            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13c8f29313caabd768df'), 'fullplot': \"Six New Yorkers juggle love, friendship, and the keenly challenging specter of adulthood. Sam Wexler is a struggling writer who's having a particularly bad day. When a young boy gets separated from his family on the subway, Sam makes the questionable decision to bring the child back to his apartment and thus begins a rewarding, yet complicated, friendship. Sam's life revolves around his friends-Annie, whose self-image keeps her from commitment; Charlie and Mary Catherine, a couple whose possible move to Los Angeles tests their relationship; and Mississippi, a cabaret singer who catches Sam's eye.\", 'imdb': {'rating': 6.8, 'votes': 24430, 'id': 1481572}, 'year': 2010, 'plot': 'Captures a generational moment - young people on the cusp of truly growing up, tiring of their reflexive cynicism, each in their own ways struggling to connect and define what it means to love and be loved.', 'genres': ['Comedy', 'Drama', 'Romance'], 'rated': 'R', 'metacritic': 45, 'title': 'Happythankyoumoreplease', 'lastupdated': '2015-08-20 00:08:34.127000000', 'languages': ['English'], 'writers': ['Josh Radnor (screenplay)'], 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'website': 'http://happythankyoumoreplease.com', 'viewer': {'rating': 3.4, 'numReviews': 6838, 'meter': 60}, 'dvd': datetime.datetime(2011, 6, 21, 0, 0), 'critic': {'rating': 5.1, 'numReviews': 52, 'meter': 40}, 'boxOffice': '$0.2M', 'rotten': 31, 'production': 'Hannover House', 'lastUpdated': datetime.datetime(2015, 9, 11, 18, 30, 57), 'fresh': 21}, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BNTk3NDgwODQ5NF5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTcwMTY5MjMzNA@@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'num_mflix_comments': 0, 'released': datetime.datetime(2011, 3, 3, 0, 0), 'awards': {'wins': 1, 'nominations': 3, 'text': '1 win & 3 nominations.'}, 'countries': ['USA'], 'cast': ['Malin Akerman', 'Michael Algieri', 'Bram Barouh', 'Dana Barron'], 'directors': ['Josh Radnor'], 'runtime': 100}\n",
