            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13c8f29313caabd78dbf'), 'plot': 'A young man, separated from his family in WWII, disguises himself as a Nazi SS Officer and uncovers more than just his family whereabouts.', 'genres': ['Action', 'Drama', 'History'], 'runtime': 124, 'metacritic': 44, 'rated': 'PG-13', 'cast': ['Jonas Armstrong', 'Ben Kingsley', 'Hannah Tointon', 'Simon Kunz'], 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BNzUwOTg4MDg0MF5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTgwMTI1NzQyMTE@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'Walking with the Enemy', 'fullplot': 'A powerful new film inspired by a true story. This feature follows the heroic lives of a world leader and a young man swept up in the horrors of WWII. Both men are from Hungary--a country and German ally that had been spared the atrocities orchestrated by Hitler throughout much of Europe. As the war reaches its climax, Germany begins to doubt the loyalties of the Hungarian leadership-in particular Regent Horthy (Academy Award winner Ben Kingsley). The Regent tries to navigate his country between the growing terror of Nazi Germany and the oppressive threat of communist Russia. He is ultimately faced with ceding power to another political party or accepting the execution of his son. As the crisis unfolds, thousands of his citizens are forced underground or put into ghettos. One of them is a young man named Elek Cohen (Jonas Armstrong) who is separated from his family and determined to find them. Aided by the woman he loves (Hannah Tointon), Elek disguises himself as a Nazi SS officer and discovers the truth of Hitler\\'s \"Final Solution.\" In a race against time to save his family and thousands of his countrymen, he embarks on a journey filled with suspense and danger. An inspirational film of love, war, and sacrifice, WALKING WITH THE ENEMY is an unforgettable experience for audiences.', 'languages': ['English', 'German', 'Hungarian', 'Romanian'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2013, 10, 13, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Mark Schmidt'], 'writers': ['Kenny Golde (screenplay)', 'Richard Lasser (additional screenplay material)'], 'awards': {'wins': 1, 'nominations': 0, 'text': '1 win.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-19 00:46:10.970000000', 'year': 2013, 'imdb': {'rating': 5.4, 'votes': 435, 'id': 1515208}, 'countries': ['Romania', 'Hungary', 'Canada', 'USA'], 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'website': 'http://www.walkingwiththeenemy.com/', 'viewer': {'rating': 3.2, 'numReviews': 1366, 'meter': 56}, 'critic': {'rating': 5.4, 'numReviews': 36, 'meter': 44}, 'boxOffice': '$0.4M', 'consensus': \"While Walking With the Enemy tells a stirring and little-known true story, it's ultimately too heavy-handed to fully resonate.\", 'rotten': 20, 'production': 'Liberty Studios', 'lastUpdated': datetime.datetime(2015, 8, 26, 18, 59, 47), 'fresh': 16}, 'num_mflix_comments': 0}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13c8f29313caabd78b36'), 'plot': \"After 42 years, feisty and delightful lesbian couple Edie and Thea are finally getting married. From the early '60s to the present day, the tireless community activists persevere through ...\", 'genres': ['Documentary', 'Drama', 'Romance'], 'runtime': 61, 'cast': ['Thea Spyer', 'Edea Windsor'], 'num_mflix_comments': 0, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMTkzMDY4NTEzNV5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTcwMTIyNjIwNA@@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'Edie & Thea: A Very Long Engagement', 'fullplot': \"After 42 years, feisty and delightful lesbian couple Edie and Thea are finally getting married. From the early '60s to the present day, the tireless community activists persevere through many battles, both personal and political. As Edie says, We just went on with this talent we have for wrestling joy from the shit. Susan Muska and Greta Olafsdottir (THE BRANDON TEENA STORY) return with a love story of two remarkable women whose commitment to each other is an inspiration to us all.\", 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2009, 6, 21, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Susan Muska', 'Grèta Olafsdèttir'], 'awards': {'wins': 1, 'nominations': 1, 'text': '1 win & 1 nomination.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-09-14 11:06:41.690000000', 'year': 2009, 'imdb': {'rating': 7.8, 'votes': 283, 'id': 1512779}, 'countries': ['USA'], 'type': 'movie'}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13c8f29313caabd78d6f'), 'plot': 'At 10 years old, Chico Colvard accidentally shot his older sister in the leg. This seemingly random act detonated a chain reaction that exposed unspeakable realities and shattered his ...', 'genres': ['Documentary', 'Family'], 'runtime': 80, 'metacritic': 65, 'title': 'Family Affair', 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMjI3MDc0Nzg2M15BMl5BanBnXkFtZTcwNDY3OTY2Mw@@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'countries': ['USA'], 'fullplot': \"At 10 years old, Chico Colvard accidentally shot his older sister in the leg. This seemingly random act detonated a chain reaction that exposed unspeakable realities and shattered his family. Thirty years later, Colvard ruptures veils of secrecy and silence again. As he bravely visits his relatives, what unfolds is a personal film that's as uncompromising, raw, and cathartic as any in the history of the medium. Driving the story forward is Colvard's sensitive probing of a complex dynamic: the way his three sisters survived severe childhood abuse by their father and, as adults, manage to muster loyalty to him. These unforgettable, invincible women paint a picture of their harrowing girlhoods as they resiliently struggle with present-day fallout. The distance time gives them from their trauma yields piercing insights about the legacy of abuse, the nature of forgiveness, and eternal longing for family and love. These truths may be too searing to bear, but they reverberate powerfully within each of us\", 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2010, 1, 7, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Chico Colvard'], 'writers': ['Chico Colvard'], 'awards': {'wins': 0, 'nominations': 1, 'text': '1 nomination.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-09-07 01:07:25.943000000', 'year': 2010, 'imdb': {'rating': 7.3, 'votes': 154, 'id': 1515059}, 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'website': 'http://www.c-linefilms.com/the_movie_2.html', 'viewer': {'rating': 4.0, 'numReviews': 85, 'meter': 80}, 'criti