            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13c9f29313caabd7b296'), 'plot': 'A climber goes on a hike and becomes trapped.', 'genres': ['Adventure', 'Biography', 'Drama'], 'runtime': 94, 'metacritic': 82, 'rated': 'R', 'cast': ['James Franco', 'Kate Mara', 'Amber Tamblyn', 'Sean Bott'], 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMTc2NjMzOTE3Ml5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTcwMDE0OTc5Mw@@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': '127 Hours', 'fullplot': \"127 Hours is the true story of mountain climber Aron Ralston's remarkable adventure to save himself after a fallen boulder crashes on his arm and traps him in an isolated canyon in Utah. Over the next five days Ralston examines his life and survives the elements to finally discover he has the courage and the wherewithal to extricate himself by any means necessary, scale a 65 foot wall and hike over eight miles before he can be rescued. Throughout his journey, Ralston recalls friends, lovers, family, and the two hikers he met before his accident. Will they be the last two people he ever had the chance to meet?\", 'languages': ['English', 'Italian'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2011, 1, 28, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Danny Boyle'], 'writers': ['Danny Boyle (screenplay)', 'Simon Beaufoy (screenplay)', 'Aron Ralston (book)'], 'awards': {'wins': 35, 'nominations': 128, 'text': 'Nominated for 6 Oscars. Another 29 wins & 128 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-31 00:00:52.747000000', 'year': 2010, 'imdb': {'rating': 7.6, 'votes': 255793, 'id': 1542344}, 'countries': ['USA', 'UK'], 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'website': 'http://www.127hoursmovie.com/', 'viewer': {'rating': 4.0, 'numReviews': 93520, 'meter': 85}, 'dvd': datetime.datetime(2011, 3, 1, 0, 0), 'critic': {'rating': 8.3, 'numReviews': 216, 'meter': 93}, 'boxOffice': '$18.3M', 'consensus': \"As gut-wrenching as it is inspirational, 127 Hours unites one of Danny Boyle's most beautifully exuberant directorial efforts with a terrific performance from James Franco.\", 'rotten': 15, 'pro