            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13caf29313caabd7ccdc'), 'plot': 'Almost as soon as Jake and Cassie decide to get married on Christmas Eve, complications arise. Ex-con Leon Deeks arrives in town, and Jake is asked by the mayor to make him his top priority...', 'genres': ['Drama', 'Family', 'Fantasy'], 'runtime': 83, 'rated': 'TV-PG', 'cast': ['Catherine Bell', 'Chris Potter', 'Catherine Disher', 'Peter MacNeill'], 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMTg1NTY3MTgyN15BMl5BanBnXkFtZTgwMzAzNDA2MDE@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': \"The Good Witch's Gift\", 'fullplot': \"Almost as soon as Jake and Cassie decide to get married on Christmas Eve, complications arise. Ex-con Leon Deeks arrives in town, and Jake is asked by the mayor to make him his top priority. At the same time, Jake's having trouble securing the wedding license since he can't find Cassie's documents proving her existence. There's also the difficulty in finding a wedding cake at the last minute. Last but not least, Jake's kids are upset: Brandon wants to spend time with his new girlfriend, and is feuding with his sister Lori. Meanwhile, Lori manages to lose Cassie's wedding ring.\", 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2010, 11, 13, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Craig Pryce'], 'writers': ['Rod Spence', 'G. Ross Parker'], 'awards': {'wins': 0, 'nominations': 2, 'text': '2 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-21 00:38:50.500000000', 'year': 2010, 'imdb': {'rating': 7.3, 'votes': 802, 'id': 1560779}, 'countries': ['Canada'], 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'viewer': {'rating': 3.6, 'numReviews': 145, 'meter': 63}, 'dvd': datetime.datetime(2014, 6, 16, 0, 0), 'lastUpdated': datetime.datetime(2015, 9, 12, 17, 19, 45)}, 'num_mflix_comments': 0}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13caf29313caabd7cd7b'), 'plot': 'After 60 years of silence, the survivors of the Chosin Reservoir Campaign of the Korean War take us on an emotional and heart-pounding journey through one of the most savage battles in American history.', 'genres': ['Documentary', 'History', 'War'], 'runtime': 86, 'title': 'Chosin', 'num_mflix_comments': 0, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMjIxMzY1NDMxNV5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTgwOTAzNDA2MDE@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'countries': ['USA'], 'fullplot': \"In the winter of 1950, 15,000 U.S. Soldiers and Marines were surrounded and trapped by an overwhelming force of communist Chinese soldiers in the frozen mountains of North Korea. Facing impossible odds, the men fought 78 miles to freedom and saved the lives of 98,000 civilian refugees. Chosin is the first-ever documentary on the Chosin Reservoir Campaign. Presented in full, immersive HD, the stories of our veterans are supplemented with rare black and white and color archival footage gathered from hundreds of hours of research. After 60 years of silence, the survivors of the campaign take us on an emotional and heart-pounding journey through one of the most savage battles in American history. These first-hand accounts, combined with footage never before seen by most Americans, create a visceral, emotionally charged experience unlike that provided by any other war documentary. As a fellow combat veteran, director Brian Iglesias forged a unique connection with the men he interviewed. Time and time again, these men shared stories that they have never told to anyone...not their wives, their children, or their closest friends. Chosin is not the first documentary to give a voice to America's veterans, but the depth of its emotional access is unlike anything previously brought to the screen.\", 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2010, 9, 10, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Brian Iglesias'], 'writers': ['Brian Iglesias', 'Anton Sattler'], 'awards': {'wins': 1, 'nominations': 0, 'text': '1 win.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-02-21 00:15:10.540000000', 'year': 2010, 'imdb': {'rating': 8.3, 'votes': 172, 'id': 1561406}, 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'viewer': {'rating': 4.4, 'numReviews': 91, 'meter': 90}, 'website': 'http://www.frozenchosin.com/', 'production': 'Post Factory Films', 'lastUpdated': datetime.datetime(2015, 9, 17, 17, 16, 17)}}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13caf29313caabd7ceea'), 'plot': 'A fictional account of events during the Philippine-American War.', 'genres': ['Drama', 'War'], 'runtime': 124, 'metacritic': 63, 'rated': 'R', 'cast': ['Arthur Acuèa', 'Irma Adlawan', 'John Arcilla', 'Merlin Bonning'], 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BNTM3NjY3NTA2N15BMl5BanBnXkFtZTcwMzEzNDE5NQ@@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'Amigo', 'fullplot': \"AMIGO, the 17th feature film from Academy Award-nominated writer-director John Sayles, stars legendary Filipino actor Joel Torre as Rafael, a village mayor caught in the murderous crossfire of the Philippine-American War. When U.S. troops occupy his village, Rafael comes under pressure from a tough-as-nails officer (Chris Cooper) to help the Americans in their hunt for Filipino guerilla fighters. But Rafael's brother (Ronnie Lazaro) is the head of the local guerillas, and considers anyone who cooperates with the Americans to be a traitor. Rafael quickly finds himself forced to make the impossible, potentially deadly decisions faced by ordinary civilians in an occupied country. A powerful drama of friendship, betrayal, romance and heartbreaking violence, AMIGO is a page torn from the untold history of the Philippines, and a mirror of today's unresolvable conflicts.\", 'languages': ['English', 'Filipino'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2011, 7, 6, 0, 0), 'directors': ['John Sayles'], 'writers': ['John Sayles'], 'awards': {'wins': 1, 'nominations': 9, 'text': '1 win & 9 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-30 00:10:41.820000000', 'year': 2010, 'imdb': {'rating': 5.7, 'votes': 460, 'id': 1562847}, 'countries': ['USA'], 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'website': 'http://www.amigomovie.com', 'viewer': {'rating': 3.4, 'numReviews': 439, 'meter': 54}, 'critic': {'rating': 6.2, 'numReviews': 45, 'meter': 62}, 'boxOffice': '$0.2M', 'rotten': 17, 'production': 'Variance Films', 'lastUpdated': datetime.datetime(2015, 9, 15, 17, 53, 8), 'fresh