            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13caf29313caabd7d634'), 'plot': 'The Khmer Rouge slaughtered nearly two million people in the late 1970s. Yet the Killing Fields of Cambodia remain unexplained. Until now. Enter Thet Sambath, an unassuming, yet cunning, ...', 'genres': ['Documentary'], 'runtime': 93, 'cast': ['Thet Sambath', 'Nuon Chea', 'Pol Pot', 'Khieu Samphan'], 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BNTAzODUyNDg2OV5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTcwMDY5ODc2NQ@@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'Enemies of the People', 'fullplot': \"The Khmer Rouge slaughtered nearly two million people in the late 1970s. Yet the Killing Fields of Cambodia remain unexplained. Until now. Enter Thet Sambath, an unassuming, yet cunning, investigative journalist who spends a decade of his life gaining the trust of the men and women who perpetrated the massacres. From the foot soldiers who slit throats to Pol Pot's right-hand man, the notorious Brother Number Two, Sambath records shocking testimony never before seen or heard. Having neglected his own family for years, Sambath's work comes at a price. But his is a personal mission. He lost his parents and his siblings in the Killing Fields. Amidst his journey to discover why his family died, we come to understand for the first time the real story of Cambodia's tragedy.\", 'languages': ['English', 'Khmer'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2010, 7, 30, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Rob Lemkin', 'Thet Sambath'], 'writers': ['Rob Lemkin', 'Thet Sambath'], 'awards': {'wins': 6, 'nominations': 5, 'text': '6 wins & 5 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-07-04 00:13:51.020000000', 'year': 2009, 'imdb': {'rating': 7.8, 'votes': 355, 'id': 1568328}, 'countries': ['UK', 'Cambodia'], 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'viewer': {'rating': 4.2, 'numReviews': 62}, 'production': 'International Film Circuit', 'lastUpdated': datetime.datetime(2015, 5, 21, 18, 7, 8)}, 'num_mflix_comments': 0}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13caf29313caabd7d63d'), 'plot': 'Director Tamra Davis pays homage to her friend in this definitive documentary but also delves into Basquiat as an iconoclast. His dense, bebop-influenced neoexpressionist work emerged while...', 'genres': ['Documentary'], 'runtime': 88, 'metacritic': 74, 'cast': ['Jean Michel Basquiat', 'Julian Schnabel', 'Larry Gagosian', 'Bruno Bischofberger'], 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMjI0MzY1MTg2MV5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTcwMTExOTE2Mw@@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'Jean-Michel Basquiat: The Radiant Child', 'fullplot': \"Director Tamra Davis pays homage to her friend in this definitive documentary but also delves into Basquiat as an iconoclast. His dense, bebop-influenced neoexpressionist work emerged while minimalist, conceptual art was the fad; as a successful black artist, he was constantly confronted by racism and misconceptions. Much can be gleaned from insider interviews and archival footage, but it is Basquiat's own words and work that powerfully convey the mystique and allure of both the artist and the man.\", 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2011, 4, 12, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Tamra Davis'], 'writers': ['Eric Martin', 'Lois Vossen'], 'awards': {'wins': 1, 'nominations': 1, 'text': '1 win & 1 nomination.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-09-05 00:41:24.963000000', 'year': 2010, 'imdb': {'rating': 7.9, 'votes': 1174, 'id': 1568335}, 'countries': ['USA'], 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'website': 'http://www.jean-michelbasquiattheradiantchild.com', 'viewer': {'rating': 4.0, 'numReviews': 703, 'meter': 86}, 'dvd': datetime.datetime(2010, 11, 9, 0, 0), 'critic': {'rating': 7.4, 'numReviews': 34, 'meter': 85}, 'boxOffice': '$0.3M', 'rotten': 5, 'production': 'Arthouse Pictures', 'lastUpdated': datetime.datetime(2015, 9, 10, 19, 19, 53), 'fresh': 29}, 'num_mflix_comments': 0}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13caf29313caabd7d706'), 'plot': \"A Moscow college student's gift car from his parents turns out to be more than anyone expects when it flies, which he uses to become both a city guardian and a speedy floral delivery boy.\", 'genres': ['Action', 'Sci-Fi', 'Thriller'], 'runtime': 102, 'cast': ['Grigoriy Dobrygin', 'Ekaterina Vilkova', 'Viktor Verzhbitskiy', 'Valeriy Zolotukhin'], 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BNjk4NjkzOTUzMV5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTgwMDUzNDA2MDE@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'Chernaya Molniya', 'fullplot': 'Moscow, 2004, and wealthy entrepreneur Kuptsov drills deep beneath the city, trying to reach a huge diamond vein. Aware that his ruthless drilling will destroy the city and its denizens, it\\'s a result he\\'s willing to accept for untold additional wealth. Fortunately, his equipment lacks enough power. He needs the Nano-catalyst (developed years ago) to fuel his machinery, but its current whereabouts is unknown. Meanwhile, in another part of the city, college boy Dima dreams of owning a car and dating gorgeous co-ed Nastya. His wealthy friend Max has a Mercedes Benz and is flirting with Nastya, which frustrates Dima. On his birthday, Dima finally gets a car (from his parents) - a grungy, antiquated Volga of which he is privately ashamed; but, unbeknownst to anyone, the car - the recipient of \"failed\" Nano-catalysis - is capable of much more, and turns Dima into an unidentified crusader of justice known as Black Lightning.', 'languages': ['Russian'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2009, 12, 31, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Dmitriy Kiselev', 'Aleksandr Voytinskiy'], 'writers': ['Dmitriy Aleynikov', 'Alexander Talal', 'Aleksandr Voytinskiy (idea)', 'Mikhail Vrubel (idea)', 'Dmitriy Aleynikov (idea)', 'Rostislav Krivitskiy (participation)', 'Vladimir Neklyudov (participation)'], 'awards': {'wins': 0, 'nominations': 1, 'text': '1 nomination.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-09-07 01:02:58.227000000', 'year': 2009,