            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13cbf29313caabd7efd6'), 'plot': 'A story based on the life of journalist Torgny Segerstedt, who alerted the Swedish public to the threat of Fascism in the 1930s.', 'genres': ['Biography', 'Drama'], 'runtime': 126, 'metacritic': 60, 'cast': ['Jesper Christensen', 'Pernilla August', 'Ulla Skoog', 'Bjèrn Granath'], 'num_mflix_comments': 2, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMTc4NzU4NzgxMF5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTgwNjQ4NzIwMjE@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'The Last Sentence', 'fullplot': \"Torgny Segerstedt was one of the leading journalists in Sweden in the 20th century. He fought a one man battle against Hitler and the Nazi regime until his death in 1945 and during these tumultuous times his private life was marked by a world in chaos, as he falls in love with his friend's wife while married himself. THE LAST SENTENCE weaves together the story of a psychological love story with a portrayal of the political situation Sweden found itself in during the Second World War. A gripping, dramatic and poetic tale about a man, who could not be silenced.\", 'languages': ['Swedish'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2014, 6, 20, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Jan Troell'], 'writers': ['Kenne Fant (book)', 'Klaus Rifbjerg (screenplay)', 'Jan Troell (screenplay)'], 'awards': {'wins': 3, 'nominations': 6, 'text': '3 wins & 6 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-09-10 17:13:55.017000000', 'year': 2012, 'imdb': {'rating': 6.0, 'votes': 421, 'id': 1590013}, 'countries': ['Sweden', 'Norway'], 'type': 'movie'}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13cbf29313caabd7f35e'), 'plot': 'Leo is immediately set adrift by his new found responsibilities as a single parent, a feeling that is made doubly distressing when Dafne, herself understandably confused and heartbroken by ...', 'genres': ['Drama'], 'runtime': 101, 'cast': ['Juan Diego Botto', 'Josè Luis Gèmez', 'Ana Risueèo', 'Pedro Alonso'], 'num_mflix_comments': 0, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMjMzMjk2MzE0Nl5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTcwNzg0MjQ5Mw@@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'Todo lo que tè quieras', 'fullplot': 'Leo is immediately set adrift by his new found responsibilities as a single parent, a feeling that is made doubly distressing when Dafne, herself understandably confused and heartbroken by her mother\\'s absence, asks for an \"artificial\" mother to help her fall asleep at night. It is here that Maèas takes the road less traveled, but to write any more about the plot line he introduces would be unfair to both the viewer and filmmaker alike. Suffice it to say that Leo\\'s actions are both surprising and potentially dangerous, as they require Leo to subsume his own identity to the point where he nearly loses it', 'languages': ['Spanish'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2010, 9, 10, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Achero Maèas'], 'writers': ['Achero Maèas'], 'awards': {'wins': 0, 'nominations': 1, 'text': '1 nomination.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-09-01 00:43:45.693000000', 'year': 2010, 'imdb': {'rating': 6.6, 'votes': 362, 'id': 1592534}, 'countries': ['Spain'], 'type': 'movie'}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13cbf29313caabd7f237'), 'plot': 'A family looks to prevent evil spirits from trapping their comatose child in a realm called The Further.', 'genres': ['Drama', 'Horror', 'Mystery'], 'runtime': 103, 'metacritic': 52, 'rated': 'PG-13', 'cast': ['Patrick Wilson', 'Rose Byrne', 'Ty Simpkins', 'Lin Shaye'], 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMTYyOTAxMDA0OF5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTcwNzgwNTc1NA@@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'Insidious', 'fullplot': 'A gripping story of a family in search of help for their son, Dalton, who fell into a coma after a mysterious incident in the attic. Little do they know that there is much more to this endless sleep than meets the eye as they explore the paranormal, and rediscover the past; the key to getting their son back once and for all.', 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2011, 4, 1, 0, 0), 'directors': ['James Wan'], 'writers': ['Leigh Whannell'], 'awards': {'wins': 9, 'nominations': 13, 'text': '9 wins & 13 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-09-03 00:38:22.710000000', 'year': 2010, 'imdb': {'rating': 6.8, 'votes': 177164, 'id': 1591095}, 'countries': ['USA', 'Canada'], 'type': 'movie', 'num_mflix_comments': 0}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13cbf29313caabd7f7e7'), 'plot': 'Dominic Toretto and his crew of street racers plan a massive heist to buy their freedom while in the sights of a powerful Brazilian drug lord and a dangerous federal agent.', 'genres': ['Action', 'Crime', 'Thriller'], 'runtime': 131, 'metacritic': 67, 'rated': 'PG-13', 'cast': ['Vin Diesel', 'Paul Walker', 'Jordana Brewster', 'Tyrese Gibson'], 'num_mflix_comments': 0, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMTUxNTk5MTE0OF5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTcwMjA2NzY3NA@@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'Fast Five', 'fullplot': \"Former cop Brian O'Conner partners with ex-con Dom Toretto on the opposite side of the law. Since Brian and Mia Toretto broke Dom out of custody, they've blown across many borders to elude authorities. Now backed into a corner in Rio de Janeiro, they must pull one last job in order to gain their freedom. As they assemble their elite team of top racers, the unlikely allies know their only shot of getting out for good means confronting the corrupt businessman who wants them dead. But he's not the only one on their tail. Hard-nosed federal agent Luke Hobbs never misses his target. When he is assigned to track down Dom and Brian, he and his strike team launch an all-out assault to capture them. But as his men tear through Brazil, Hobbs learns he can't separate the good guys from the bad. Now, he must rely on his instincts to corner his prey... before someone else runs them down first.\", 'languages': ['English', 'Portuguese', 'Spanish', 'Italian'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2011, 4, 29, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Justin Lin'], 'writers': ['Chris Morgan', 'Gary Scott Thompson (characters)'], 'awards': {'wins': 8, 'nominations': 19, 'text': '8 wins & 19 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-09-12 00:01:36.217000000', 'year': 2011, 'imdb': {'rating': 7.4, 'votes': 260163, 'id': 1596343}, 'countries': ['USA'], 'type': 'movie'}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13cbf29313caabd7f840'), 'plot': 'A young lawyer travels to a remote village where he discovers the vengeful ghost of a scorned woman is terrorizing the locals.', 'genres': ['Drama', 'Horror', 'Thriller'], 'runtime': 95, 'metacritic': 62, 'rated': 'PG-13', 'cast': ['Emma Shorey', 'Molly Harmon', 'Ellisa Walker-Reid', 'Sophie Stuckey'], 'num_mflix_comments': 0, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMjEwMzIxOTg3N15BMl5BanBnXkFtZTcwMjI4ODUzNw@@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'The Woman in Black', 'fullplot': 'In London, lawyer Arthur Kipps still grieves the death of his beloved wife Stella on the delivery of their son Joseph four years ago. His employer gives him a last chance to keep his job, and he is assigned to travel to the remote village of Cryphin Gifford to examine the documentation of the Eel Marsh House that belonged to the recently deceased Mrs. Drablow. Arthur befriends Daily on the train and the man offers a ride to him to the Gifford Arms inn. Arthur has a cold reception and the owner of the inn tells that he did not receive the request of reservation and there is no available room. The next morning, Arthur meets solicitor Jerome who advises him to return to London. However, Arthur goes to the isolated manor and soon he finds that Eel Marsh House is haunted by the vengeful ghost of a woman dressed in black. He also learns that the woman lost her son drowned in the marsh and she seeks revenge, taking the children of the scared locals.', 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2012, 2, 3, 0, 0), 'directors': ['James Watkins'], 'writers': ['Susan Hill (novel)', 'Jane Goldman (screenplay)'], 'awards': {'wins': 7, 'nominations': 9, 'text': '7 wins & 9 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-09-05 01:01:25.463000000', 'year': 2012, 'imdb': {'rating': 6.5, 'votes': 129284, 'id': 1596365}, 'countries': ['UK', 'Canada', 'Sweden'], 'type': 'movie'}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13cbf29313caabd7fbc9'), 'plot': 'Bertrand Tavernier is in top form with this gripping, superbly mounted drama set against the savage Catholic/Protestant wars that ripped France apart in the 16th century. Based on a novella...', 'genres': ['Action', 'Drama', 'History'], 'runtime': 139, 'metacritic': 78, 'cast': ['Mèlanie Thierry', 'Lambert Wilson', 'Gaspard Ulliel', 'Grègoire Leprince-Ringuet'], 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BYjJiYjU5ZTctNjBlZC00OWY3LWExNzctYmI3NDgwNDBjMDdjXkEyXkFqcGdeQXVyODIyOTEyMzY@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'The Princess of Montpensier', 'fullplot': \"Bertrand Tavernier is in top form with this gripping, superbly mounted drama set against the savage Catholic/Protestant wars that ripped France apart in the 16th century. Based on a novella by the celebrated Madame de Lafayette, the action centers on the love of Marie de Mezières for her dashing cousin Henri de Guise, thwarted when her father's political ambitions force her into marriage with the well-connected Philippe de Montpensier, who she has never met. When Philippe is called away to fight, she is left in the care of Count Chabannes, an aging nobleman with a disdain for warfare, and soon becomes exposed to the sexual and political intrigues of court.\", 'languages': ['French'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2010, 11, 3, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Bertrand Tavernier'], 'writers': ['Jean Cosmos', 'Madame de La Fayette (short story)', 'Franèois-Olivier Rousseau', 'Bertrand Tavernier'], 'awards': {'wins': 2, 'nominations': 9, 'text': '2 wins & 9 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-24 01:11:10.493000000', 'year': 2010, 'imdb': {'rating': 6.5, 'votes': 2578, 'id': 1599975}, 'countries': ['France', 'Germany'], 'type': 'movie', 'num_mflix_comments': 0}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13cbf29313caabd7fc55'), 'plot': 'A thriller centered on a young man who sets out to uncover the truth about his life after finding his baby photo on a missing persons website.', 'genres': ['Action', 'Mystery', 'Thriller'], 'runtime': 106, 'metacritic': 25, 'rated': 'PG-13', 'cast': ['Alfred Molina', 'Maria Bello', 'Jason Isaacs', 'Denzel Whitaker'], 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMTkxNzU3OTg0Nl5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTcwNDY5MDY2Ng@@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'Abduction', 'fullplot': 'High school seniors Nathan and Karen find a website with photos of children who are missing or believed abducted. One of the photos is of Nathan as a child, putting into question the identities of the couple whom he\\'s always called Mom and Dad. Contacting the site to learn more only results in Nathan becoming the target of an intense, high-tech, international manhunt. Before his \"parents\" can explain themselves, they are executed by hired guns, and Nathan is on the run with Karen in tow (who just happened to be there at the wrong time). Phone use by either of them only connects directly to a man claiming to be C.I.A., in whom they find reasons not to trust. With encroaching shootouts, car chases, hand-to-hand combat and explosions around them, this seems quite much for a mere case of child abduction, and Nathan can only rely on the wrestling, boxing and martial arts skills taught by his \"dad\" to protect both himself and Karen as they follow a lead to find Martin, Nathan\\'s biological father, who can likely shed light on what all this is about.', 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2011, 9, 23, 0, 0), 'directors': ['John Singleton'], 'writers': ['Shawn Christensen'], 'awards': {'wins': 2, 'nominations': 3, 'text': '2 wins & 3 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-17 00:03:41.640000000', 'year': 2011, 'imdb': {'rating': 5.0, 'votes': 60924, 'id': 1600195}, 'countries': ['USA'], 'type': 'movie', 'num_mflix