            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13cbf29313caabd81332'), 'plot': 'Dave is a married man with three kids and a loving wife, and Mitch is a single man who is at the prime of his sexual life. One fateful night while Mitch and Dave are peeing in a fountain, lightning strikes and they switch bodies.', 'genres': ['Comedy'], 'runtime': 112, 'metacritic': 39, 'rated': 'R', 'cast': ['Ryan Reynolds', 'Jason Bateman', 'Leslie Mann', 'Olivia Wilde'], 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMTk3NTM4NDg3OF5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTcwNDk3MzEwNQ@@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'The Change-Up', 'fullplot': \"Growing up together, Mitch (Ryan Reynolds) and Dave (Jason Bateman) were inseparable best friends, but as the years have passed they've slowly drifted apart. While Dave is an overworked lawyer, husband and father of three, Mitch has remained a single, quasi-employed man-child who has never met a responsibility he liked. To Mitch, Dave has it all: beautiful wife Jamie (Leslie Mann), kids who adore him and a high-paying job at a prestigious law firm. To Dave, living Mitch's stress-free life without obligation or consequence would be a dream come true. Following a drunken night out together, Mitch and Dave's worlds are turned upside down when they wake up in each other's bodies and proceed to freak out. Despite the freedom from their normal routines and habits, the guys soon discover that each other's lives are nowhere near as rosy as they once seemed. Further complicating matters are Dave's sexy legal associate, Sabrina (Olivia Wilde) and Mitch's estranged father (Alan Arkin). With time not on their side, Mitch and Dave comically struggle to avoid completely destroying each other's lives before they can find a way to get their old ones back.\", 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2011, 8, 5, 0, 0), 'directors': ['David Dobkin'], 'writers': ['Jon Lucas', 'Scott Moore'], 'awards': {'wins': 0, 'nominations': 2, 'text': '2 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-31 16:20:27.443000000', 'year': 2011, 'imdb': {'rating': 6.4, 'votes': 129060, 'id': 1488555}, 'countries': ['USA'], 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'website': 'http://www.thechangeupmovie.com', 'viewer': {'rating': 3.2, 'numReviews': 45519, 'meter': 47}, 'dvd': datetime.datetime(2011, 11, 8, 0, 0), 'critic': {'rating': 4.4, 'numReviews': 148, 'meter': 25}, 'boxOffice': '$37.0M', 'consensus': \"There's a certain amount of fun to be had from watching Bateman and Reynolds play against type, but it isn't enough to carry The Change-Up through its crude humor and formulaic plot.\", 'rotten': 111, 'production': 'Universal Pictures', 'lastUpdated': datetime.datetime(2015, 9, 14, 21, 15, 58), 'fresh': 37}, 'num_mflix_comments': 0}\n",
