            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13cdf29313caabd84c22'), 'plot': \"In modern-day Paris, a journalist finds her life becoming entwined with a young girl whose family was torn apart during the notorious Vel' d'Hiv Roundup in 1942.\", 'genres': ['Drama', 'War'], 'runtime': 111, 'metacritic': 59, 'rated': 'PG-13', 'cast': ['Kristin Scott Thomas', 'Mèlusine Mayance', 'Niels Arestrup', 'Frèdèric Pierrot'], 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMTYyMzEyNzMxM15BMl5BanBnXkFtZTcwNzA5ODI1NQ@@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': \"Sarah's Key\", 'fullplot': \"One of the darkest moments in French history occurred in 1942 Paris when French officials rounded up over 10,000 Jews and placed them in local camps. Eventually over 8,000 were sent off to German concentration camps. As 10-year old Sarah and her family are being arrested, she hides her younger brother in a closet. After realizing she will not be allowed to go home, Sarah does whatever she can to get back to her brother. In 2009, a journalist named Julia is on assignment to write a story on the deported Jews in 1942. When she moves into her father-in-law's childhood apartment, she realizes it once belonged to the Strazynski family, and their daughter Sarah.\", 'languages': ['French', 'English', 'Italian', 'German', 'Yiddish'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2011, 7, 22, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Gilles Paquet-Brenner'], 'writers': ['Tatiana De Rosnay (novel)', 'Serge Joncour (screenplay)', 'Gilles Paquet-Brenner (screenplay)'], 'awards': {'wins': 4, 'nominations': 4, 'text': '4 wins & 4 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-19 00:15:52.063000000', 'year': 2010, 'imdb': {'rating': 7.5, 'votes': 11700, 'id': 1668200}, 'countries': ['France'], 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'website': 'http://www.sarahskey.com.au/', 'viewer': {'rating': 3.9, 'numReviews': 9212, 'meter': 83}, 'dvd': datetime.datetime(2011, 11, 22, 0, 0), 'critic': {'rating': 6.4, 'numReviews': 112, 'meter': 72}, 'boxOffice': '$7.7M', 'consensus': \"Sarah's Key is an absorbing, impeccably-acted Holocaust drama with minor plot issues.\", 'rotten': 31, 'production': 'The Weinstein Company', 'lastUpdated': datetime.datetime(2015, 9, 1, 19, 32, 36), 'fresh': 81}, 'num_mflix_comments': 0}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13cdf29313caabd8475a'), 'plot': 'Werner Herzog gains exclusive access to film inside the Chauvet caves of Southern France and captures the oldest known pictorial creations of humanity.', 'genres': ['Documentary', 'History'], 'runtime': 90, 'metacritic': 86, 'rated': 'G', 'cast': ['Werner Herzog', 'Jean Clottes', 'Julien Monney', 'Jean-Michel Geneste'], 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMTYxNDExMzUwMl5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTcwNjM2MzYwNQ@@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'Cave of Forgotten Dreams', 'fullplot': 'In 1994, a group of scientists discovered a cave in Southern France perfectly preserved for over 20,000 years and containing the earliest known human paintings. Knowing the cultural significance that the Chauvet Cave holds, the French government immediately cut-off all access to it, save a few archaeologists and paleontologists. But documentary filmmaker, Werner Herzog, has been given limited access, and now we get to go inside examining beautiful artwork created by our ancient ancestors around 32,000 years ago. He asks questions to various historians and scientists about what these humans would have been like and trying to build a bridge from the past to the present.', 'languages': ['English', 'German', 'French'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2011, 8, 31, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Werner Herzog'], 'writers': ['Werner Herzog'], 'awards': {'wins': 10, 'nominations': 18, 'text': '10 wins & 18 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-29 00:27:19.890000000', 'year': 2010, 'imdb': {'rating': 7.4, 'votes': 10017, 'id': 1664894}, 'countries': ['Canada', 'USA', 'France', 'Germany', 'UK'], 'type': 'movie', 'num_mflix_comments': 0}\n",
