            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13cdf29313caabd8548e'), 'fullplot': \"Kyle and Sarah Miller have it all: a huge gated house on the water, fancy cars, and the potential for romance in their relationship. He's just back from a business trip (he brokers diamonds) and their teen daughter Avery is sneaking out to a party, when four thugs in security uniforms and ski masks stage a home invasion. They want what's in the safe: cash and diamonds. Kyle stalls them, trying to negotiate for Sarah's freedom. Over the next few hours, the back stories of the four robbers (two brothers, a girlfriend, and the representative of a local drug kingpin) as well as the fault lines in Kyle and Sarah's marriage come into play. Is there room here for heroism?\", 'imdb': {'rating': 5.3, 'votes': 32027, 'id': 1674784}, 'year': 2011, 'plot': \"As they're held for ransom, a husband and wife's predicament grows more dire amid the discovery of betrayal and deception.\", 'genres': ['Crime', 'Drama', 'Thriller'], 'rated': 'R', 'metacritic': 37, 'title': 'Trespass', 'lastupdated': '2015-09-13 00:42:51.137000000', 'languages': ['English'], 'writers': ['Karl Gajdusek'], 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'website': 'http://www.trespass-the-movie.com/', 'viewer': {'rating': 2.5, 'numReviews': 7026, 'meter': 22}, 'dvd': datetime.datetime(2011, 11, 1, 0, 0), 'critic': {'rating': 3.3, 'numReviews': 70, 'meter': 10}, 'boxOffice': '$16.8k', 'consensus': 'Another claustrophobic thriller that Joel Schumacher can churn out in his sleep, Trespass is nasty and aggressive, more unpleasant than entertaining.', 'rotten': 63, 'production': 'Millennium Entertainment', 'lastUpdated': datetime.datetime(2015, 9, 16, 20, 33, 42), 'fresh': 7}, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMTM4NTc0Mzk5N15BMl5BanBnXkFtZTcwNDA4NDUyNg@@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'num_mflix_comments': 0, 'released': datetime.datetime(2011, 10, 21, 0, 0), 'awards': {'wins': 0, 'nominations': 2, 'text': '2 nominations.'}, 'countries': ['USA',