            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13cef29313caabd87200'), 'fullplot': \"The independent and lonely hunter Martin David is hired by the powerful biotech company Red Leaf to hunt down the last Tasmanian tiger. Red Leaf is interested in the DNA of the animal and Martin travels to Tasmania alone. He poses as a researcher from a university and lodges in the house of Lucy Armstrong. Martin learns that Lucy's husband has been missing for a long time and he befriends her children, Sass and Bike. When Martin goes to the village, he has a hostile reception from the locals. Along the days, Martin spends his days in the Tasmanian wilderness chasing the Tiger and becomes closer and closer to the Armstrong family. But Red Leaf wants results no matter the costs.\", 'imdb': {'rating': 6.8, 'votes': 27630, 'id': 1703148}, 'year': 2011, 'plot': 'Martin, a mercenary, is sent from Europe by a mysterious biotech company to the Tasmanian wilderness on a hunt for the last Tasmanian tiger.', 'genres': ['Adventure', 'Drama', 'Thriller'], 'rated': 'R', 'metacritic': 63, 'title': 'The Hunter', 'lastupdated': '2015-09-07 00:04:26.620000000', 'languages': ['English'], 'writers': ['Alice Addison (screenplay)', 'Wain Fimeri (original adaptation)', 'Daniel Nettheim (original adaptation)', 'Julia Leigh (based on the novel by)'], 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'website': 'http://www.magpictures.com/thehunter/', 'viewer': {'rating': 3.5, 'numReviews': 15766, 'meter': 62}, 'dvd': datetime.datetime(2012, 7, 3, 0, 0), 'critic': {'rating': 6.4, 'numReviews': 85, 'meter': 69}, 'boxOffice': '$0.2M', 'consensus': 'The Hunter occasionally suffers from predictability, but Willem Dafoe gives a terrific performance as an obsessive hunter on the trail of a mysterious beast.', 'rotten': 26, 'production': 'Magnolia Pictures', 'lastUpdated': datetime.datetime(2015, 9, 13, 18, 15, 2), 'fresh': 59}, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BNTI4Mzc0MTg4OV5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTcwNTc1NDQzNw@@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jp