            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13cff29313caabd897e8'), 'plot': 'A journalist, who is more of an activist teams up with the sister of a murdered model, as she gets interested in the case and wants to bring justice to her case.', 'genres': ['Crime', 'Drama', 'Thriller'], 'runtime': 136, 'cast': ['Rani Mukerji', 'Vidya Balan', 'Myra Karn', 'Neil Bhoopalam'], 'num_mflix_comments': 0, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMTU4Mzk0NDY3OV5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTcwMjE1MTkyNA@@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'No One Killed Jessica', 'fullplot': \"Devastated when she is told that that her sister, Jessica Lall, is shot dead by Manish Bhardwaj, the son of Pramod, a Congress party Member of Parliament in Haryana, Delhi-based Sabrina Lall, in the company of her parents, attends the Court to view a charade that will lead to the acquittal of the accused and his accomplices seven years after the incident. Disillusioned by rampart police corruption and inefficiency; a stagnant British introduced legal system; the passing of her mother & the hospitalization of her father, she retreats unto herself. Then foul-mouthed NDTV employee, Meera Gaity, known for being more of an activist than a Journalist, takes an interest in this incident, and uncovers conspiracy & corruption that led to the accused' acquittals - leading to a near India-wide protest. While preparing herself to participate in a candle-lit procession at Delhi's India Gate, Meera will confront Sabrina and will come to know the reasons why the latter refuses to be involved in this situation any more.\", 'languages': ['Hindi', 'English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2011, 1, 7, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Raj Kumar Gupta'], 'writers': ['Amitabh Bhattacharya (lyrics)', 'Raj Kumar Gupta (story)'], 'awards': {'wins': 1, 'nominations': 9, 'text': '1 win & 9 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-21 00:40:03.453000000', 'year': 2011, 'imdb': {'rating': 7.2, 'votes': 6320, 'id': 1734110}, 'countries': ['India'], 'type': 'mov