            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13cff29313caabd89d1f'), 'plot': 'The digital revolution of the last decade has unleashed creativity and talent of people in an unprecedented way, unleashing unlimited creative opportunities. But does democratized culture ...', 'genres': ['Documentary', 'Music'], 'runtime': 80, 'cast': ['èlafur Arnalds', 'Scott Belsky', 'Robyn Carlsson', 'Mike Cosola'], 'num_mflix_comments': 1, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMTY1OTI0NzUxNl5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTcwNjI4NDM4NA@@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'PressPausePlay', 'fullplot': \"The digital revolution of the last decade has unleashed creativity and talent of people in an unprecedented way, unleashing unlimited creative opportunities. But does democratized culture mean better art, film, music and literature or is true talent instead flooded and drowned in the vast digital ocean of mass culture? Is it cultural democracy or mediocrity? This is the question addressed by PressPausePlay, a documentary film containing interviews with some of the world's most influential creators of the digital era.\", 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2011, 3, 1, 0, 0), 'directors': ['David Dworsky', 'Victor Kèhler'], 'awards': {'wins': 2, 'nominations': 1, 'text': '2 wins & 1 nomination.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-09-06 00:03:55.823000000', 'year': 2011, 'imdb': {'rating': 7.6, 'votes': 1309, 'id': 1737674}, 'countries': ['Sweden', 'Australia', 'France', 'USA', 'Iceland', 'Japan', 'Germany', 'Spain', 'Norway', 'UK'], 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'viewer': {'rating': 3.9, 'numReviews': 231, 'meter': 80}, 'website': 'http://www.presspauseplay.com/', 'production': 'FilmBuff', 'lastUpdated': datetime.datetime(2015, 7, 16, 18, 35, 13)}}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13cff29313caabd89d6e'), 'plot': \"Apple. Intel. Genentech. Atari. Google. Cisco. Stratospheric successes with high stakes all around. Behind some of the world's most revolutionary companies are a handful of men who (through...\", 'genres': ['Documentary', 'Biography', 'History'], 'runtime': 84, 'cast': ['Bill Bowes', 'Herbert Boyer', 'Po Bronson', 'Nolan Bushnell'], 'num_mflix_comments': 0, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMjA1ODE1MjU3MV5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTcwMDMyOTQ0NA@@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'Something Ventured', 'fullplot': \"Apple. Intel. Genentech. Atari. Google. Cisco. Stratospheric successes with high stakes all around. Behind some of the world's most revolutionary companies are a handful of men who (through timing, foresight, a keen ability to size up other people, and a lot of luck) saw opportunity where others did not: these are the original venture capitalists. All were backing and building companies before the term 'venture capital' had been coined: companies that led to the birth of biotechnology and the spectacular growth in microprocessors, personal computers and the web. SOMETHING VENTURED uncovers the ups and downs of the building of some of the greatest companies of the twentieth century, and the hidden dramas behind some of the most famous names in business.\", 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2011, 4, 24, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Daniel Geller', 'Dayna Goldfine'], 'awards': {'wins': 0, 'nominations': 1, 'text': '1 nomination.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-01 00:01:13.500000000', 'year': 2011, 'imdb': {'rating': 7.0, 'votes': 393, 'id': 1737747}, 'countries': ['USA'], 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'viewer': {'rating': 3.9, 'numReviews': 109, 'meter': 78}, 'dvd': datetime.datetime(2014, 12, 8, 0, 0), 'production': 'Zeitgeist Films', 'lastUpdated': datetime.datetime(2015, 8, 23, 18, 36, 50)}}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13cff29313caabd89dc9'), 'plot': \"In order to immortalize his love, a groom decides to create conflict between his and his to-be bride's families.\", 'genres': ['Comedy', 'Drama', 'Family'], 'countries': ['India'], 'cast': ['Supriya Pathak', 'Anang Desai', 'Rajeev Mehta', 'Nimisha Vakharia'], 'num_mflix_comments': 1, 'title': 'Khichdi: The Movie', 'fullplot': \"Narrated through the two wise kids of the hilariously madcap Parekh family, namely Jacky and Chakki. Khichdi - The movie is about a hare brained dream of a snail brained bunch of lovable losers. Hansa's brother Himanshu has born a ridiculous ambition that is to have a memorable legendary love story. It's all together another matter that he is not in love with anyone and neither is he capable of getting any sensible girl smitten to him. But as Babuji over wisely says that for every idiotic Praful there is an even more idiotic Hansa made, his prophecy turns out to be true. Parminder, Himanshu's neighbor falls in love with Himanshu for no logical reason and the 2 get engaged to get married. That's when this ridiculous story line takes a ridiculous turn. Himanshu realizes on the eve of the wedding that the impending ceremony would mean impending doom to his desire to have a legendary love story. For nothing interesting ever happened in his love story to make it memorable. It was a simple non happening take with a boring happy ending. No resistance, no conflict, no separation, no sad song, no climax nothing. And so our gifted dumb family sets out to stall the wedding. And then begins their journey to create all those missing stages in Himanshu's love story in order to make it legendary. How, in this hilariously hare brained process, they make a mess of everything and how at the incredibly ridiculous climax Himanshu eventually manages to win his love back, makes up the story of Khichdi The Movie.\", 'languages': ['Hindi'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2010, 10, 1, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Aatish Kapadia'], 'writers': ['Aatish Kapadia (screenplay)'], 'awards': {'wins': 0, 'nominations': 1, 'text': '1 nomination.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-19 00:25:57.673000000', 'year': 2010, 'imdb': {'rating': 7.1, 'votes': 974, 'id': 1738293}, 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'viewer': {'rating': 2.9, 'numReviews': 48, 'meter': 33}, 'lastUpdated': datetime.datetime(2015, 8, 13, 19, 49, 21)}}\n",
