            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13d1f29313caabd8f761'), 'plot': 'The story of an unlikely friendship between a bear, Ernest, and a young mouse named Celestine.', 'genres': ['Animation', 'Comedy', 'Drama'], 'runtime': 80, 'metacritic': 86, 'rated': 'PG', 'cast': ['Forest Whitaker', 'Lambert Wilson', 'Pauline Brunner', 'Mackenzie Foy'], 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMjA3NzA5ODY4M15BMl5BanBnXkFtZTgwMzU5ODMwMTE@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'Ernest & Celestine', 'fullplot': 'There is a world of where the Bears live above ground in their cities and the rodents live below in in their underground ones in mutual fear and hate. However, Celestine, an apprentice mouse dentist, finds at least momentary common cause with Ernest, a poor street Bear musician, that gets them rejected from both their respective worlds. In spite of this misfortune, the exiles find a growing friendship between themselves as their respective talents flower because of it. Despite this, their quietly profound challenge to the founding prejudices of their worlds cannot be ignored as the authorities track them down. When that happens, Ernest and Celestine must stand up for their love in the face of such bigotry and achieve the impossible.', 'languages': ['French'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2014, 2, 28, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Stèphane Aubier', 'Vincent Patar', 'Benjamin Renner'], 'writers': ['Gabrielle Vincent (book)', 'Daniel Pennac (screenplay)'], 'awards': {'wins': 16, 'nominations': 10, 'text': 'Nominated for 1 Oscar. Another 15 wins & 10 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-09-04 00:00:31.883000000', 'year': 2012, 'imdb': {'rating': 7.9, 'votes': 9795, 'id': 1816518}, 'countries': ['France', 'Belgium', 'Luxembourg'], 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'website': 'http://www.ernestandcelestine.com', 'viewer': {'rating': 4.1, 'numReviews': 6854, 'meter': 88}, 'dvd': datetime.datetime(2014, 6, 17, 0, 0), 'critic': {'rating': 8.2, 'numReviews': 75, 'meter': 97}, 'boxOffice': 