            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13d1f29313caabd90336'), 'plot': 'This is the story of companies who engineered their products to fail.', 'genres': ['Documentary'], 'runtime': 75, 'cast': ['Molly Malcolm', 'Marcos Lèpez', 'Lynn Owens', 'Richard Jones'], 'num_mflix_comments': 0, 'title': 'The Light Bulb Conspiracy', 'fullplot': \"Once upon a time..... products were made to last. Then, at the beginning of the 1920s, a group of businessmen were struck by the following insight: 'A product that refuses to wear out is a tragedy of business' (1928). Thus Planned Obsolescence was born. Shortly after, the first worldwide cartel was set up expressly to reduce the life span of the incandescent light bulb, a symbol for innovation and bright new ideas, and the first official victim of Planned Obsolescence. During the 1950s, with the birth of the consumer society, the concept took on a whole new meaning, as explained by flamboyant designer Brooks Stevens: 'Planned Obsolescence, the desire to own something a little newer, a little better, a little sooner than is necessary...'. The growth society flourished, everybody had everything, the waste was piling up (preferably far away in illegal dumps in the Third World) - until consumers started rebelling... Can the modern growth society survive without Planned Obsolescence? Did the eternal light bulb ever exist? How can a tiny chip 'kill' a product? How did two artists from New York manage to extend the lives of millions of iPods? Is Planned Obsolescence itself becoming obsolete?\", 'languages': ['English', 'French', 'Catalan', 'German', 'Spanish'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2010, 12, 16, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Cosima Dannoritzer'], 'writers': ['Cosima Dannoritzer'], 'awards': {'wins': 2, 'nominations': 3, 'text': '2 wins & 3 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-09-10 17:56:53.103000000', 'year': 2010, 'imdb': {'rating': 8.1, 'votes': 1400, 'id': 1825163}, 'countries': ['Spain', 'France'], 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'viewer': {'rating': 4.2, 'numReviews': 13}, 'website': 'http://www.facebook.com/pages/The-Light-Bulb-Conspiracy/181469828550173?ref=sgm', 'lastUpdated': datetime.datetime(2015, 9, 12, 17, 23, 27)}}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13d1f29313caabd90811'), 'plot': \"From pagan re-enactors to failed communes, black metal festivals to Arctic hermits, and the forever Golden Hour to the Northern Lights, 'A Spell to Ward off the Darkness' is an inquiry into...\", 'genres': ['Documentary'], 'runtime': 98, 'metacritic': 70, 'cast': ['Robert Aiki Aubrey Lowe'], 'num_mflix_comments': 1, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BNzQ0MTQ0NjgyMl5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTgwODE0NTcwNjE@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'A Spell to Ward Off the Darkness', 'fullplot': \"From pagan re-enactors to failed communes, black metal festivals to Arctic hermits, and the forever Golden Hour to the Northern Lights, 'A Spell to Ward off the Darkness' is an inquiry into the possibilities of a spiritual existence within an increasingly secular Western culture. A participatory ethnography in the best possible sense, A SPELL choreographs the actions of non-actors within existing Scandinavian landscapes in an effort to arrive at a hybrid document of the past, present, and future; it is a record of experience that proposes belief in transcendence as a viable outcome of living in the now.\", 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2015, 3, 18, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Ben Rivers', 'Ben Russell'], 'writers': ['Ben Rivers', 'Ben Russell'], 'awards': {'wins': 1, 'nominations': 3, 'text': '1 win & 3 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-24 00:22:45.510000000', 'year': 2013, 'imdb': {'rating': 6.0, 'votes': 268, 'id': 1828124}, 'countries': ['France', 'Estonia', 'Germany'], 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'website': 'http://www.aspelltowardoffthedarkness.com/', 'viewer': {'rating': 2.7, 'numReviews': 104, 'meter': 41}, 'critic': {'rating': 6.7, 'numReviews': 16, 'meter': 88}, 'lastUpdated': datetime.datetime(2015, 9, 12, 18, 24, 7), 'rotten': 2, 'production': 'Rouge International', 'fresh': 14}}\n",
