            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13d2f29313caabd923d9'), 'plot': \"Follows John McCain's 2008 presidential campaign, from his selection of Alaska Governor Sarah Palin as his running mate to their ultimate defeat in the general election.\", 'genres': ['Biography', 'Drama', 'History'], 'runtime': 118, 'rated': 'TV-MA', 'cast': ['Julianne Moore', 'Woody Harrelson', 'Ed Harris', 'Peter MacNicol'], 'num_mflix_comments': 0, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMTQwNjkzNzg4NV5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTcwODIxMTM0Nw@@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'Game Change', 'fullplot': \"Summer, 2008: John McCain secures the nomination, but polls behind Barack Obama. Strategist Steve Schmidt suggests a game changer: picking a conservative female with media savvy, unknown Alaska governor Sarah Palin, as vice president. She's an immediate hit and a quick study - the gap closes. Then, Tina Fey's impersonation, a raft of criticism, and missing her family send Palin into a near-catatonic state: she doesn't prepare for her Katie Couric interview and bombs. Schmidt searches for an answer: don't expect her to learn the issues, but give her a script. Palin does well in the debate with Biden; she finds her voice, goes off script, and goes rogue. A mistake?\", 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2012, 3, 10, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Jay Roach'], 'writers': ['Danny Strong', 'Mark Halperin (book)', 'John Heilemann (book)'], 'awards': {'wins': 26, 'nominations': 33, 'text': 'Won 3 Golden Globes. Another 23 wins & 33 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-20 00:19:10.720000000', 'year': 2012, 'imdb': {'rating': 7.4, 'votes': 16068, 'id': 1848902}, 'countries': ['USA'], 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'website': 'http://www.hbo.com/#/movies/game-change/index.html', 'viewer': {'rating': 3.7, 'numReviews': 2109, 'meter': 76}, 'dvd': datetime.datetime(2013, 1, 8, 0, 0), 'critic': {'rating': 6.9, 'numReviews': 37, 'meter': 65}, 'lastUpdated': datetime.datetime(2015, 9, 14, 18, 12