            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13d5f29313caabd9cb11'), 'plot': 'Set during the second Manchu invasion of Korea, Nam Yi, the best archer in Korea, goes up against the Qing Dynasty to save his younger sister Ja In - who was dragged away by Manchurian.', 'genres': ['Action', 'History'], 'runtime': 122, 'rated': 'R', 'cast': ['Hae-il Park', 'Seung-ryong Ryu', 'Mu-Yeol Kim', 'Chae-won Moon'], 'num_mflix_comments': 1, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMTgwMjAyNzA0N15BMl5BanBnXkFtZTcwMTcxOTIwNw@@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'War of the Arrows', 'fullplot': \"Two children Nam-yi and Ja-in are being chased by King Injo's guards and saved by their father Choi Pyeong-ryung, an officer of King Gwanghae and a skilled archer. He sends his own children to find a place of refuge with his best friend Kim Mu-seon. As they escape crying, Ja-in begs her brother to go back to their father but their father is killed in front of Nam-yi. Nam-yi, though bitten by the guard dogs, kills them and escapes with Ja-in. Nam-yi becomes the only family Ja-in has. 13 years later Nam-yi is now a skilled archer and hunter. He learns from Mu-seon's son Seo-goon that he and Ja-in plan to get married, with the approval of Mu-seon who is also Ja-in's godfather. During the wedding, Nam-yi is up in the mountains hunting deer. He hears the rumble of the invading forces. When Nam-yi makes it back to the village, he finds his step-father slaughtered and his sister taken away. Nam-yi then sets out to find the Qing army and take out their army with his bow.\", 'languages': ['Korean'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2011, 8, 10, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Han-min Kim'], 'writers': ['Han-min Kim (screenplay)'], 'awards': {'wins': 7, 'nominations': 11, 'text': '7 wins & 11 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-09-12 00:28:09.123000000', 'year': 2011, 'imdb': {'rating': 7.2, 'votes': 7815, 'id': 2025526}, 'countries': ['South Korea'], 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'website': 'http://www.arrow201