            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13dbf29313caabdafef0'), 'plot': 'A biography of Daisy and Violet Hilton, conjoined twins who started as \"freaks\" in side shows, then went on to be stars of Vaudeville and films.', 'genres': ['Documentary'], 'runtime': 95, 'metacritic': 68, 'cast': ['Lea Thompson', 'Nancy Allen', 'Timothy Stack', 'Blake Boyd'], 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMjE4NjU2MzkyNl5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTgwMzUzMjA4MTE@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'Bound by Flesh', 'fullplot': 'This remarkable documentary tells the amazing story of Daisy and Violet Hilton, conjoined twins who rose to superstardom at the beginning of the 20th century as sideshow attractions, performing alongside the likes of Bob Hope and Charlie Chaplin. Ruthlessly exploited by their managers, the sisters ultimately sued for their freedom-which they won at a terrible cost. Bound By Flesh puts a touchingly human face on two outsiders who went from the lowest rungs of society to the big time and back again.', 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2012, 10, 19, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Leslie Zemeckis'], 'writers': ['Leslie Zemeckis'], 'awards': {'wins': 1, 'nominations': 1, 'text': '1 win & 1 nomination.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-07 00:01:25.960000000', 'year': 2012, 'imdb': {'rating': 6.4, 'votes': 290, 'id': 2357003}, 'countries': ['USA'], 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'website': 'http://www.boundbyflesh.com/', 'viewer': {'rating': 3.5, 'numReviews': 213, 'meter': 56}, 'dvd': datetime.datetime(2014, 10, 27, 0, 0), 'critic': {'rating': 7.1, 'numReviews': 14, 'meter': 93}, 'lastUpdated': datetime.datetime(2015, 8, 19, 19, 29, 9), 'rotten': 1, 'production': 'Sundance Selects', 'fresh': 13}, 'num_mflix_comments': 0}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13dbf29313caabdaffd8'), 'plot': 'A look at the early career of Wikileaks founder, Julian Assange.', 'genres': ['Biography', 'Drama'], 'runtime': 89, 'cast': ['Rachel Griffiths', 'Anthony LaPaglia', 'Alex Williams', 'Laura Wheelwright'], 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMTYxMTg4MTIzOF5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTgwODUwNDM1MDE@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'Underground: The Julian Assange Story', 'fullplot': \"Julian Assange is one of the most significant figures of the twenty first century. But before he was famous, before WikiLeaks, before the internet even existed, he was a teenage computer hacker in Melbourne. This is his story. In 1989, known as 'Mendax', Assange and two friends formed a group called the 'International Subversives'. Using early home computers and defining themselves as 'white hat hackers' - those who look but don't steal - they broke into some of the world's most powerful and secretive organisations. They were young, brilliant, and in the eyes of the US Government, a major threat to national security. At the urging of the FBI, the Australian Federal Police set up a special taskforce to catch them. But at a time when most Australian police had never seen a computer, let alone used one, they had to figure out just where to begin. Police ingenuity and old-fashioned detective work are pitted against nimble, highly skilled young men in this new crime frontier. What follows, is a tense and gripping game of cat and mouse through the electronic underground of Melbourne.\", 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2012, 10, 7, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Robert Connolly'], 'writers': ['Suelette Dreyfus (book)', 'Robert Connolly (adaptation)'], 'awards': {'wins': 1, 'nominations': 5, 'text': '1 win & 5 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-09-05 00:25:12.470000000', 'year': 2012, 'imdb': {'rating': 6.8, 'votes': 1336, 'id': 2357453}, 'countries': ['Australia'], 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'viewer': {