            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13dbf29313caabdafb40'), 'plot': 'A 36 foot crocodile goes on the rampage in Beijing after being moved from a peaceful Crocodile Farm and onto the menu of a local gangster.', 'genres': ['Action', 'Comedy', 'Horror'], 'runtime': 90, 'rated': 'PG-13', 'cast': ['Tao Guo', 'Barbie Hsu', 'Suet Lam'], 'num_mflix_comments': 0, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMTQxMjExNjU5Ml5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTgwMjg3MjIwMDE@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'Croczilla', 'fullplot': \"Xiao, befriends Amao a 36 foot crocodile, who lives on his fathers croc sanctuary. Xiao's father is forced to sell his crocodiles to a gangster who plans to use them for high priced meals. Before Amao is due to be slaughtered, he escapes, slaying his captors in the process. Amongst the chaos, Amao accidentally swallows a bag with $1 million dollars inside. When rumor's of this spread, the town locals are split with some fearing for their lives and others set out to capture and kill the crocodile, at any cost.\", 'countries': ['China'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2012, 6, 8, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Li Sheng Lin'], 'writers': ['Li Sheng Lin'], 'awards': {'wins': 1, 'nominations': 0, 'text': '1 win.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-24 00:17:12.917000000', 'year': 2012, 'imdb': {'rating': 4.1, 'votes': 423, 'id': 2354196}, 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'viewer': {'rating': 2.0, 'numReviews': 27, 'meter': 17}, 'dvd': datetime.datetime(2013, 2, 12, 0, 0), 'lastUpdated': datetime.datetime(2015, 8, 31, 18, 52, 24)}}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13dbf29313caabdafb3c'), 'plot': \"To many, Don McCullin is the greatest living war photographer, often cited as an inspiration for today's photojournalists. For the first time, McCullin speaks candidly about his ...\", 'genres': ['Documentary'], 'countries': ['UK'], 'cast': ['Harold Evans', 'Don McCullin', 'Michael Parkinson', 'Sue Ryder'], 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMjMzMTUwNjc5OF5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTgwMDQ1NDAxMzE@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'McCullin', 'fullplot': \"To many, Don McCullin is the greatest living war photographer, often cited as an inspiration for today's photojournalists. For the first time, McCullin speaks candidly about his three-decade career covering wars and humanitarian disasters on virtually every continent and the photographs that often defined historic moments. From 1969 to 1984, he was the Sunday Times of London's star photographer, where he covered stories from the civil war in Cyprus to the war in Vietnam, from the man-made famine in Biafra to the plight of the homeless in the London of the swinging sixties. Exploring not only McCullin's life and work, but how the ethos of journalism has changed throughout his career, the film is a commentary on the history of photojournalism told through the lens of one of its most acclaimed photographers.\", 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2013, 1, 1, 0, 0), 'directors': ['David Morris', 'Jacqui Morris'], 'awards': {'wins': 3, 'nominations': 0, 'text': 'Nominated for 2 BAFTA Film Awards. Another 1 win.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-09-14 12:56:09.810000000', 'year': 2012, 'imdb': {'rating': 8.1, 'votes': 880, 'id': 2354205}, 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'website': 'http://www.facebook.com/pages/McCullin-Feature-Documentary-Film/131058970341083', 'viewer': {'rating': 4.4, 'numReviews': 183}, 'critic': {'rating': 7.3, 'numReviews': 14, 'meter': 100}, 'lastUpdated': datetime.datetime(2015, 9, 10, 19, 6, 9), 'rotten': 0, 'fre