            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13dbf29313caabdb07c1'), 'plot': '1936. The Spanish Civil War broke out and the Anarchist militia occupy the Lower Aragon. A Matarranya, Ramon and his wife Dora hide a secret ancestral to all other villagers. Near the ...', 'genres': ['Drama', 'Fantasy'], 'countries': ['Spain'], 'cast': ['èlex Brendemèhl', 'Maria Molins', 'Tom Sizemore', 'Pere Ponce'], 'num_mflix_comments': 0, 'title': 'El bosc', 'fullplot': '1936. The Spanish Civil War broke out and the Anarchist militia occupy the Lower Aragon. A Matarranya, Ramon and his wife Dora hide a secret ancestral to all other villagers. Near the farmhouse where they live, twice a year become visible some mysterious lights that come from the surrounding forest. According to family tradition, the lights illuminate a door leading into another world, where no one can bring back. What is truth in the legend when they find out an anarchist in love with Dora seeks a solution with Ramon and disappears through the light.', 'languages': ['Catalan', 'Spanish', 'English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2012, 12, 14, 0, 0), 'directors': ['èscar Aibar'], 'writers': ['Albert Sènchez Pièol'], 'awards': {'wins': 1, 'nominations': 11, 'text': '1 win & 11 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-06-03 01:09:34.933000000', 'year': 2012, 'imdb': {'rating': 5.4, 'votes': 185, 'id': 2364649}, 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'viewer': {'rating': 4.5, 'numReviews': 1}, 'lastUpdated': datetime.datetime(2015, 6, 26, 20, 7, 19)}}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13dbf29313caabdb0230'), 'plot': 'A look at the early career of Wikileaks founder, Julian Assange.', 'genres': ['Biography', 'Drama'], 'runtime': 89, 'cast': ['Rachel Griffiths', 'Anthony LaPaglia', 'Alex Williams', 'Laura Wheelwright'], 'num_mflix_comments': 1, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMTYxMTg4MTIzOF5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTgwODUwNDM1MDE@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'Underground: The Julian Assange Story', 'fullplot': \"Julian Assange is one of the most significant figures of the twenty first century. But before he was famous, before WikiLeaks, before the internet even existed, he was a teenage computer hacker in Melbourne. This is his story. In 1989, known as 'Mendax', Assange and two friends formed a group called the 'International Subversives'. Using early home computers and defining themselves as 'white hat hackers' - those who look but don't steal - they broke into some of the world's most powerful and secretive organisations. They were young, brilliant, and in the eyes of the US Government, a major threat to national security. At the urging of the FBI, the Australian Federal Police set up a special taskforce to catch them. But at a time when most Australian police had never seen a computer, let alone used one, they had to figure out just where to begin. Police ingenuity and old-fashioned detective work are pitted against nimble, highly skilled young men in this new crime frontier. What follows, is a tense and gripping game of cat and mouse through the electronic underground of Melbourne.\", 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2012, 10, 7, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Robert Connolly'], 'writers': ['Suelette Dreyfus (book)', 'Robert Connolly (adaptation)'], 'awards': {'wins': 1, 'nominations': 5, 'text': '1 win & 5 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-09-16 21:45:16.653000000', 'year': 2012, 'imdb': {'rating': 6.8, 'votes': 1345, 'id': 2357453}, 'countries': ['Australia'], 'type': 'movie',