            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13def29313caabdb54d5'), 'plot': \"A chronicle of James Brown's rise from extreme poverty to become one of the most influential musicians in history.\", 'genres': ['Biography', 'Drama', 'Music'], 'runtime': 139, 'metacritic': 71, 'rated': 'PG-13', 'cast': ['Chadwick Boseman', 'Nelsan Ellis', 'Dan Aykroyd', 'Viola Davis'], 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMTY1NjAyMTUzMl5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTgwMTM4NzQ4MTE@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'Get on Up', 'fullplot': \"On route to the stage, singer James Brown recalls a life with a turbulent childhood where music was his only constructive release for his passions. A chance demonstration of that in prison led to a new friend who helped get him out and into a musical career. With his fire and creative daring, Brown became a star who defiantly created new possibilities in show business both on and behind the stage in face of racism and conventional thinking. Along the way, James would also become a peacemaker who redefined and raised the African-American community's feeling of self-worth when it was needed most. However, those same domineering passions would lead James Brown alienating everyone around him as his appetites became ever more self-destructive. Only after he hit rock bottom with a serious mistake does Brown realize what he needs to do make his life as the Godfather of Soul truly worthwhile.\", 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2014, 8, 1, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Tate Taylor'], 'writers': ['Jez Butterworth (screenplay)', 'John-Henry Butterworth (screenplay)', 'Steven Baigelman (story)', 'Jez Butterworth (story)', 'John-Henry Butterworth (story)'], 'awards': {'wins': 5, 'nominations': 15, 'text': '5 wins & 15 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-25 00:02:43.320000000', 'year': 2014, 'imdb': {'rating': 6.9, 'votes': 12626, 'id': 2473602}, 'countries': ['USA', 'UK'], 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'website': 'http://www.getonupmovie.com/', 'viewer