            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13dff29313caabdb824d'), 'plot': 'The secret relationship between a student and a teacher, will their love last?', 'genres': ['Drama'], 'runtime': 90, 'cast': ['Jeong Eun-Chae', 'Sun-kyun Lee', 'Joon-sang Yoo', 'Ji-won Ye'], 'num_mflix_comments': 2, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BNTg3OTkyNTgxMl5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTgwMDc0OTAxMzE@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': \"Nobody's Daughter Haewon\", 'fullplot': 'University student Hae-Won (Jung Eun-Chae) wants to break up with Teacher Sung-Joon (Lee Sun-Kyun). They have had a secret relationship. Hae-Won meets her mother (Kim Ja-Ok), who is going to emigrate to Canada tomorrow. After meeting her mother, Hae-Won feels depressed and she decides to meet Sung-Joon for the first time in a long while. On that day, Hae-Won and Sung-Joon happen to meet students at a restaurant who study the same major and their relationship becomes known to others. Hae-Won becomes more depressed. Sung-Joon then suggests they runaway to somewhere else.', 'languages': ['Korean', 'English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2013, 2, 28, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Sang-soo Hong'], 'writers': ['Sang-soo Hong (screenplay)'], 'awards': {'wins': 0, 'nominations': 5, 'text': '5 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-09-02 00:08:56.727000000', 'year': 2013, 'imdb': {'rating': 6.8, 'votes': 725, 'id': 2576522}, 'countries': ['South Korea'], 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'viewer': {'rating': 3.6, 'numReviews': 89}, 'fresh': 14, 'critic': {'rating': 7.2, 'numReviews': 15, 'meter': 93}, 'rotten': 1, 'lastUpdated': datetime.datetime(2015, 7, 24, 19, 46, 19)}}\n",
