            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13dff29313caabdb8359'), 'plot': 'On February 12, 2008, in Oxnard, California, eighth-grade student Brandon McInerney shot his classmate Larry King twice in the back of the head during first period. When Larry died two days...', 'genres': ['Documentary'], 'runtime': 89, 'cast': ['James Bing', 'Jeremy Bing', 'Rosalie Black', 'Dawn Boldrin'], 'num_mflix_comments': 0, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BOTEyNDA0MDgwM15BMl5BanBnXkFtZTcwNjQzMjgzOQ@@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'Valentine Road', 'fullplot': \"On February 12, 2008, in Oxnard, California, eighth-grade student Brandon McInerney shot his classmate Larry King twice in the back of the head during first period. When Larry died two days later, his murder shocked the nation. Was this a hate crime, one perpetrated by a budding neo-Nazi whose masculinity was threatened by an effeminate gay kid who may have had a crush on him? Or was there even more to it? Looking beyond all the copious news coverage of this tragic event, Valentine Road tells the story of two victims: the deceased and the murderer. With keen insight, the film connects the human wreckage of Larry's and Brandon's troubled lives-both physically abused, both from broken homes, and both searching for a sense of belonging.\", 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2013, 10, 4, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Marta Cunningham'], 'awards': {'wins': 4, 'nominations': 6, 'text': '4 wins & 6 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-09-14 08:37:13.267000000', 'year': 2013, 'imdb': {'rating': 7.3, 'votes': 735, 'id': 2577990}, 'countries': ['USA'], 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'viewer': {'rating': 4.1, 'numReviews': 135, 'meter': 89}, 'dvd': datetime.datetime(2015, 2, 2, 0, 0), 'critic': {'rating': 7.1, 'numReviews': 10, 'meter': 90}, 'lastUpdated': datetime.datetime(2015, 6, 28, 19, 23, 33), 'rotten': 1, 'fresh': 9}}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13dff29313caabdb8732'), 'plot': \"About Twist of Faith Jacob Fisher ('David Julian Hirsh'), an Orthodox Jewish Cantor and amateur songwriter who resides in Brooklyn, New York, witnesses the senseless murder of his wife and ...\", 'genres': ['Drama'], 'runtime': 85, 'cast': ['Toni Braxton', 'David Julian Hirsh', 'Nathaniel J. Potvin', 'Paula Shaw'], 'num_mflix_comments': 0, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMzk5OGEwOTItOTllMi00MTIyLThjMDgtMzQzOTkzMTE5NWM3XkEyXkFqcGdeQXVyODU4NTYwMDA@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'Twist of Faith', 'fullplot': \"About Twist of Faith Jacob Fisher ('David Julian Hirsh'), an Orthodox Jewish Cantor and amateur songwriter who resides in Brooklyn, New York, witnesses the senseless murder of his wife and three children. Catatonic, Jacob walks out on his Jewish mourning ritual, leaving behind his Jewish garments, wallet and keys. Abandoning his identity, he wanders aimlessly, hoping somehow to understand his tragedy. Fortuitously, he lands in Brent, Alabama (population 2,500), where he is embraced by Nina (Toni Braxton), a single mother and the lead singer of a small gospel choir (an unlikely finalist in the competition to determine the best gospel choir in Alabama), her Uncle Moe (Mykelti Williamson) and their gospel community who help his return to life while music brings Nina and Jacob together as they try to make sense of his past and their possible future.\", 'languages': ['English', 'Hebrew'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2013, 2, 9, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Paul A. Kaufman'], 'writers': ['Joyce Gittlin (teleplay)', 'Janet Fattal (teleplay)', 'Stephen Tolkin (teleplay)', 'Joyce Gittlin (story)', 'Janet Fattal (story)'], 'awards': {'wins': 0, 'nominations': 5, 'text': '5 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-09-10 17:07:19.070000000', 'year': 2013, 'imdb': {'rating': 6.8, 'votes': 436, 'id': 2585068}, 'countries': ['USA'], 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'viewer': {'rating': 3.2, 'numRe