            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13e7f29313caabdc7372'), 'plot': 'Held captive and faced with their imminent executions, fifty strangers are forced to choose the one person among them who deserves to live.', 'genres': ['Drama', 'Horror', 'Sci-Fi'], 'runtime': 87, 'cast': ['Julie Benz', 'Carter Jenkins', 'Mercy Malick', 'Lisa Pelikan'], 'num_mflix_comments': 2, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMTg0Mjg0MjUwOF5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTgwNjk0NzQ4NzE@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'Circle', 'fullplot': \"In a massive, mysterious chamber, fifty strangers awaken to find themselves trapped with no memory of how they got there. Organized in an inward-facing circle and unable to move, they quickly learn that every two minutes, one of them must die... executed by a strange device in the center of the room. At first, the attacks seem random, but soon the strangers realize that they, as a group, have the power to decide who will be the next to be killed. A vote. A chance to control the machine. But how can they choose who deserves to die? And what happens when there's only one person left? Circle is a film about people, how they value one another, and what they do under the worst possible circumstances. A film about what makes us human - who we are, what we believe, and ultimately, the lengths we will go to save ourselves.\", 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2015, 5, 28, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Aaron Hann', 'Mario Miscione'], 'writers': ['Aaron Hann', 'Mario Miscione'], 'awards': {'wins': 0, 'nominations': 1, 'text': '1 nomination.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-31 00:53:40.513000000', 'year': 2015, 'imdb': {'rating': 7.2, 'votes': 26, 'id': 3118452}, 'countries': ['USA'], 'type': 'movie'}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13e7f29313caabdc6f40'), 'fullplot': '1932. Jimmy Gralton is back home in the Irish countryside after ten years of forced exile in the USA. His widowed mother Alice is happy, Jimmy\\'s friends are happy, all the young people who enjoy dancing and singing are happy. Which is not the case of Father Sheridan, the local priest, nor of the village squire, nor of Dennis O\\'Keefe, the chief of the fascists. The reason is simple: Jimmy is a socialist activist. So when the \"intruder\" reopens the village hall, thus enabling the villagers to gather to sing, dance, paint, study or box, they take a dim view of the whole thing. People who think and unite are difficult to manipulate, aren\\'t they? From that moment on they will use every means possible to get rid of Jimmy and his \"dangerous\" hall.', 'imdb': {'rating': 6.7, 'votes': 2896, 'id': 3110960}, 'year': 2014, 'plot': 'During the Depression, Jimmy Gralton returns home to Ireland after ten years of exile in America. Seeing the levels of poverty and oppression, the activist in him reawakens and he looks to re-open the dance hall that led to his deportation.', 'genres': ['Drama'], 'rated': 'PG-13', 'metacritic': 63, 'title': \"Jimmy's Hall\", 'lastupdated': '2015-08-18 00:05:47.860000000', 'languages': ['English'], 'writers': ['Paul Laverty (screenplay)', \"Donal O'Kelly (play)\"], 'type': 'movie', 'tomatoes': {'website': 'http://www.facebook.com/JimmysHallFilm', 'viewer': {'rating': 3.5, 'numReviews': 1424, 'meter': 60}, 'critic': {'rating': 6.7, 'numReviews': 82, 'meter': 77}, 'boxOffice': '$0.4M', 'consensus': \"Benefiting from a talented cast and sensitive work from director Ken Loach, Jimmy's Hall offers period drama rich with relevant sociopolitical themes.\", 'rotten': 19, 'production': 'Sony Pictures Classics', 'lastUpdated': datetime.datetime(2015, 8, 23, 18, 1, 16), 'fresh': 63}, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BNTk0NDk4MzIzMl5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTgwNjMwMTA5MTE@._V1_