            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13e8f29313caabdcb41c'), 'plot': 'A documentary around the world looking for young italians who had left the country. From Paris to London, from Bergen to Wien, from Tenerife to NY, six stories of ordinary separation, one question: what happened to Italy?', 'genres': ['Documentary', 'Biography', 'Drama'], 'runtime': 67, 'title': 'Emergency Exit: Young Italians Abroad', 'num_mflix_comments': 0, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BYWU1NTc4MjgtMzY5Zi00MDFhLTk3MmMtNDgwMzAyMjdiZTViXkEyXkFqcGdeQXVyNjUwMjUzNTU@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'countries': ['USA', 'Italy', 'UK', 'Spain', 'Norway', 'France', 'Austria'], 'fullplot': 'Emergency Exit is a documentary project about Italy and the consequences of the last 20 years of politics on the young generation: a lot of young Italian leave their country every year, more than 90% of them are graduates and professionally skilled. They move away for a lot of reasons, but nobody in Italy seems to have the desire to listen or care for them. So I decided to start a trip: I traveled around six (and more) European countries, from Paris to London, Berlin, Wien, Bergen and Tenerife, finding young italians who left Italy, looking for better opportunities of life and career.', 'languages': ['Italian'], 'cast': ['Andrea Lodovichetti', 'Alessia Gatti', 'Bill Emmott', 'Patrizia Pierazzo'], 'directors': ['Brunella Filè'], 'writers': ['Brunella Filè (creator)', 'Brunella Filè (story)', 'Brunella Filè'], 'awards': {'wins': 1, 'nominations': 1, 'text': '1 win & 1 nomination.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-01-01 00:39:28.883000000', 'year': 2014, 'imdb': {'rating': '', 'votes': '', 'id': 3251178}, 'type': 'movie'}\n",
