            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13ebf29313caabdd1b02'), 'plot': 'When he was arrested in 2008 in Thailand as a result of a U.S. government sting operation, the career of internationally known arms smuggler Viktor Bout came to a decisive end. Veiled by ...', 'genres': ['Documentary'], 'runtime': 90, 'cast': ['Alla Bout', 'Sergei Bout', 'Viktor Bout', 'Wim Brown'], 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMjEyNTE5ODI4MV5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTgwMDU3MjY1MTE@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'The Notorious Mr. Bout', 'fullplot': 'When he was arrested in 2008 in Thailand as a result of a U.S. government sting operation, the career of internationally known arms smuggler Viktor Bout came to a decisive end. Veiled by the obscurity of post-Soviet Russia, Bout had built an empire of aerial delivery so vast he was called \"the merchant of death\" and was even the subject of a Hollywood film. In sharp contrast to the widely known, super-villain persona, however, was another Bout: a philosophical businessman who simply enjoyed travel, his work, his family, and filming it all with his video camera.', 'languages': ['Russian', 'English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2014, 1, 17, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Tony Gerber', 'Maxim Pozdorovkin'], 'awards': {'wins': 0, 'nominations': 2, 'text': '2 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-18 00:13:58.923000000', 'year': 2014, 'imdb': {'rating': 6.5, 'votes': 277, 'id': 3460064}, 'countries': ['Russia', 'USA'], 'type': 'movie', 'num_mflix_comments': 0}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13ebf29313caabdd190d'), 'plot': 'When atrocities are committed in countries held hostage by ruthless dictators, Human Rights Watch sends in the E-Team (Emergencies Team), a collection of fiercely intelligent individuals ...', 'genres': ['Documentary'], 'runtime': 88, 'metacritic': 66, 'cast': ['Anna Neistat'], 'num_mflix_comments': 0, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMjI4NDExNDYxNF5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTgwMDkyOTczMTE@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'E-Team', 'fullplot': \"When atrocities are committed in countries held hostage by ruthless dictators, Human Rights Watch sends in the E-Team (Emergencies Team), a collection of fiercely intelligent individuals hired to document war crimes and report them to the rest of the world. Within this volatile climate, filmmakers Ross Kauffman and Katy Chevigny take us to the frontline in Syria and Libya, where shrapnel, bullet holes, and unmarked graves provide mounting evidence of coordinated attacks conducted by Bashar al-Assad and the now-deceased Muammar Gaddafi. The crimes are rampant, random, and often undocumented, making E-Team's effort to get information out of the country and into the hands of media outlets and criminal courts all the more necessary.\", 'languages': ['English', 'German', 'Arabic', 'Russian', 'French'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2014, 10, 22, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Katy Chevigny', 'Ross Kauffman'], 'awards': {'wins': 4, 'nominations': 3, 'text': '4 wins & 3 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-28 00:08:28.957000000', 'year': 2014, 'imdb': {'rating': 7.1, 'votes': 338, 'id': 3456090}, 'countries': ['USA'], 'type': 'movie'}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13ebf29313caabdd19d5'), 'plot': 'A comedy about Allie and Harper and their needlessly difficult journey to the beach.', 'genres': ['Comedy'], 'runtime': 98, 'metacritic': 71, 'rated': 'R', 'cast': ['Bridey Elliott', 'Clare McNulty', 'Neil Casey', 'Alysia Reiner'], 'num_mflix_comments': 2, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMjEwODMzMzkxN15BMl5BanBnXkFtZTgwNzY3NDgyNjE@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'Fort Tilden', 'fullplot': 'Fort Tilden: New York City\\'s secluded seaside nirvana where, like flies to honey, Brooklyn\\'s hip millennial set flocks on sweltering weekend afternoons for unbridled summertime indulgence. Amidst the vexing stagnation of quarter-life crises, Allie (Clare McNulty) struggles to prepare for the Peace Corps, while Harper (Bridey Elliot) awaits checks from her father to fund her artistic dreams. But the two friends quickly shun responsibilities for the day when a pair of good-looking guys invites them along for a carefree Fort Tilden afternoon. As the two young women board their fixed-gear bicycles and embark on a lengthy journey to the beach, they quickly realize that, akin to their confusing, transitioning lives, they neither know where they\\'re going nor how they plan to get there. The debut feature film of directors Sarah-Violet Bliss and Charles Rogers - and showcasing the comedic versatility of Clare McNulty and Bridey Elliott as Allie and Harper - \"Fort Tilden\" is a hilariously insightful and recognizable look at the consequences of extended adolescence.', 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2015, 8, 14, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Sarah-Violet Bliss', 'Charles Rogers'], 'writers': ['Sarah-Violet Bliss (story)', 'Sarah-Violet Bliss', 'Brian Lannin (story)', 'Charles Rogers (story)', 'Charles Rogers'], 'awards': {'wins': 2, 'nominations': 3, 'text': '2 wins & 3 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-19 00:03:19.640000000', 'year': 2014, 'imdb': {'rating': 5.3, 'votes'