            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13eff29313caabdd7413'), 'plot': \"In 2014, recreational marijuana sales began in Colorado. With all eyes on ground zero of the green rush, The Denver Post appointed the world's first marijuana editor. Pot is legal and The Cannabist is covering it as it unfolds.\", 'genres': ['Documentary', 'Comedy', 'News'], 'runtime': 79, 'title': 'Rolling Papers', 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMTQ4MjYwODUzN15BMl5BanBnXkFtZTgwMDIxNzMzNzE@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'countries': ['USA', 'Uruguay'], 'fullplot': \"In today's media, the status quo can flip so abruptly that news outlets are forced to reshape themselves. On January 1, 2014 as recreational marijuana explodes off the shelves of Colorado dispensaries, The Denver Post is telling the story. The Cannabist is the first pot section of a major newspaper and Ricardo Baca, the world's first marijuana editor sets out to report history in the making with a team of straight-laced staff writers and offbeat freelancers. Policy news, strain reviews, parenting advice and edible recipes are the new norm on a new beat: pot journalism. Legalization is an experiment for society and a risk for the dying industry of newspapers to hedge its bets on a new one.\", 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2015, 3, 15, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Mitch Dickman'], 'awards': {'wins': 1, 'nominations': 0, 'text': '1 win.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-09-10 17:48:49.450000000', 'year': 2015, 'imdb': {'rating': 5.8, 'votes': 18, 'id': 3621360}, 'type': 'movie', 'num_mflix_comments': 0}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13eff29313caabdd760c'), 'plot': \"Erik Sparrow is one of the lucky ones. He's got a good job. He's in a stable relationship. He lives in one of the greatest cities in the world. Does he deserve it? Probably not. He's not ...\", 'genres': ['Comedy', 'Horror'], 'runtime': 86, 'metacritic': 55, 'cast': ['Jonathan Caouette', 'Zach Clark', 'Dustin Guy Defa', 'Juliette Fairley'], 'num_mflix_comments': 0, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMTc3MTE3NTQ2MV5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTgwMjUxNzU4MjE@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'Summer of Blood', 'fullplot': 'Erik Sparrow is one of the lucky ones. He\\'s got a good job. He\\'s in a stable relationship. He lives in one of the greatest cities in the world. Does he deserve it? Probably not. He\\'s not too bright. He\\'s not very attractive. He\\'s not at all ambitious. He\\'s chubby and he\\'s always complaining. And when his girlfriend Jody proposes to him, he doesn\\'t even have the good sense to accept her offer. He\\'ll never find a woman like this again. Instead, Erik bumbles his way around the issue, offering one excuse after another for not getting married. When Jody dumps him and starts seeing an old flame from college, Erik tries to win her back. When he fails, he attempts to date other women, but the results are disastrous. Erik\\'s starts falling apart. His job grows more unfulfilling. He becomes obsessed with a kinky co-worker who has no interest in him. He becomes riddled with despair. One night, Erik meets an enigmatic stranger named Gavin who asks him, \"Do you want to die?\" Erik shrugs and says, \"I do.\" Then everything goes pitch black. When Erik wakes up from the darkness, he finds himself changed forever. He\\'s stronger, more confident and free to do whatever he wants. Dating is a cinch. He\\'s a Lothario, a sexual dynamo; able to seduce any women he wants without even trying. He quits his job. Finally, he\\'s free and unshackled with not a care in the world. Except for one little thing, the excruciating stomach pains. There\\'s only one remedy for that... BLOOD!', 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2014, 4, 17, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Onur Tukel'], 'writers': ['Onur Tukel'], 'awards': {'wins': 0, 'nominations': 1, 'text': '1 nomination.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-17 00:50:07.627000000', 'year': 2014, 'imdb': {'rating': 5.4, 'votes': 574, 'id': 3625352}, 'countries': ['USA'], 'type': 'movie'}\n",
