            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13f1f29313caabddb66f'), 'plot': 'The story of an all-consuming passion between a creator and his creation.', 'genres': ['Drama'], 'runtime': 90, 'cast': ['Kirill Frolov', 'Chulpan Khamatova', 'Yuliya Marchenko', 'Evgeniy Mironov'], 'title': 'Sindrom Petrushki', 'fullplot': 'Since early childhood Peter has been obsessed with the world of puppets, but his greater obsession is with a real girl, Lisa. He crafts his perfect woman out of her. But Lisa isn\\'t a docile marionette. She\\'s a living human being and she rebels against her creator. Based on the critically-acclaimed, brilliant and poignant novel by one of the best contemporary Russian writers, Dina Rubina, \"Petrushka Syndrome\" is a multidimensional metaphor, where a sense of duality pervades everything. People and dolls, life and art, the Creator and the creation depend on one another. And where does one draw the line between them?', 'languages': ['Russian'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2015, 6, 9, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Elena Hazanov'], 'writers': ['Alena Alova', 'Dina Rubina (based on the novel by)'], 'awards': {'wins': 1, 'nominations': 1, 'text': '1 win & 1 nomination.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-23 01:02:22.460000000', 'year': 2015, 'imdb': {'rating': '', 'votes': '', 'id': 3775176}, 'countries': ['Russia', 'Germany', 'Switzerland'], 'type': 'movie', 'num_mflix_comments': 0}\n",
