            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13f4f29313caabde2cea'), 'plot': 'The political drama of the fall of the Iron Curtain as told by one of its power brokers and the widow of one of its casualties.', 'genres': ['Documentary', 'History', 'Thriller'], 'runtime': 97, 'cast': ['Miklès Nèmeth', 'Gundula Schafitel', 'Mathias Rèssler', 'Uta Koch'], 'num_mflix_comments': 0, 'title': '1989', 'fullplot': \"'1989' is a creative documentary and a high-politics drama about the collapse of the Iron Curtain. A young technocrat, Miklos Nemeth, becomes Hungary's new prime minister to save the country's appalling economy. He decides to remove the expensive border control apparatus from the state budget. A young couple from East Germany is encouraged by the rumours that the Hungarian border to Austria will be opened and decide to make a go for it. But Nemeth's decision has set him up against formidable adversaries and communist hardliners. The young couple are caught up in the political power-game, and the young man is shot dead at the border. This tragic event paradoxically accelerates Nemeth's final decision to open the borders, and soon after the Berlin wall falls.\", 'languages': ['English', 'Hungarian', 'German'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2014, 11, 1, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Erzsèbet Rècz', 'Anders èstergaard'], 'writers': ['Erzsèbet Rècz', 'Anders èstergaard'], 'awards': {'wins': 0, 'nominations': 4, 'text': '4 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-06 00:20:54.037000000', 'year': 2014, 'imdb': {'rating': 7.4, 'votes': 113, 'id': 4119270}, 'countries': ['Denmark', 'Germany', 'Hungary', 'Norway'], 'type': 'movie'}\n",
