            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13f5f29313caabde4142'), 'plot': 'People tend to be intentionally provocative or extremely argumentative over petty matters on twitter. A woman who challenges men becomes targeted as a public enemy. Young men expose her ...', 'genres': ['Drama'], 'runtime': 100, 'cast': ['Yo-han Byeon', 'Lee Ju-Seung', 'Yoo-ram Bae', 'Jin-soo Byeon'], 'num_mflix_comments': 0, 'title': 'Socialphobia', 'fullplot': \"People tend to be intentionally provocative or extremely argumentative over petty matters on twitter. A woman who challenges men becomes targeted as a public enemy. Young men expose her identity and even show up on her doorstep. But what they find is MIN Ha-young, the woman who had hanged herself. What caused her death? Was it by suicide or murder? Socialphobia addresses the question of adopting a different identity on the Internet through the death of a woman. Two young men Ji-woong and Yong-min who were preparing for the police academy exam become involved in the case. What apparently looks like suicide is held under suspicion by the two as foul play. After posing the possibility of homicide, the young men return to the crime scene. However mystery itself does not seem to be the point of this film as it gradually exposes during the course of finding the truth to MIN Ha-young's death, her life as it really was and what the two men in pursuit of the real cause of her death wanted to prove.\", 'languages': ['Korean'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2015, 3, 12, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Seok-jae Hong'], 'writers': ['Seok-jae Hong'], 'awards': {'wins': 2, 'nominations': 2, 'text': '2 wins & 2 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-07-28 00:15:26.543000000', 'year': 2014, 'imdb': {'rating': 6.7, 'votes': 30, 'id': 4203200}, 'countries': ['South Korea'], 'type': 'movie'}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13f5f29313caabde3d40'), 'plot': 'An exposè of rape crimes on U.S. college campuses, their institutional cover-ups, and the devastating toll they take on students and their families.', 'genres': ['Documentary'], 'runtime': 103, 'metacritic': 77, 'rated': 'PG-13', 'cast': ['Kirby Dick', 'Amy Ziering', 'Amy Herdy', 'Annie Clark'], 'num_mflix_comments': 1, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BNjc4Mjk3ODgxMl5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTgwMjc3OTQ1NDE@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'The Hunting Ground', 'fullplot': 'From the makers of The Invisible War (2012) comes a startling exposè of rape crimes on U.S. college campuses, their institutional cover-ups and the devastating toll they take on students and their families. Weaving together veritè footage and first-person testimonies, the film follows the lives of several undergraduate assault survivors as they attempt to pursue - despite incredible push back, harassment, and traumatic aftermath - both their education and justice.', 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2015, 1, 23, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Kirby Dick'], 'writers': ['Kirby Dick'], 'awards': {'wins': 0, 'nominations': 1, 'text': '1 nomination.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-29 00:23:33.937000000', 'year': 2015, 'imdb': {'rating': 6.4, 'votes': 324, 'id': 4185572}, 'countries': ['USA'], 'type': 'movie'}\n",
