            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13f7f29313caabde6f18'), 'plot': \"The Department of Emotional Integrity (DEI) documents all relationship activity. A 'relationship score' is given to keep people accountable for their choices. The score is public for all to...\", 'genres': ['Drama', 'Romance'], 'runtime': 99, 'cast': ['Aaron Yoo', 'Brittany Ishibashi', 'Brandon Soo Hoo', 'Victoria Park'], 'num_mflix_comments': 1, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BMTQ2OTA2MjA3Nl5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTgwMDc2NjIwODE@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'Everything Before Us', 'fullplot': \"The Department of Emotional Integrity (DEI) documents all relationship activity. A 'relationship score' is given to keep people accountable for their choices. The score is public for all to see, and affects various aspects of daily life. Two couples, teenagers and early 30s, face different but intersecting challenges in their relationships within the rules of the DEI.\", 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2015, 6, 3, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Wesley Chan', 'Philip Wang'], 'writers': ['Wesley Chan', 'Chris Dinh', 'Philip Wang'], 'awards': {'wins': 1, 'nominations': 1, 'text': '1 win & 1 nomination.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-26 00:32:57.557000000', 'year': 2015, 'imdb': {'rating': 7.6, 'votes': 246, 'id': 4401704}, 'countries': ['USA'], 'type': 'movie'}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13f7f29313caabde6828'), 'plot': '(T)ERROR is the first documentary to place filmmakers on the ground during an active FBI counterterrorism sting operation. Through the perspective of \"Shariff\", a 63-year-old Black ...', 'runtime': 93, 'title': '(T)ERROR', 'num_mflix_comments': 0, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BOTYxNzI2ODA2M15BMl5BanBnXkFtZTgwNzM3NzI4NjE@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'countries': ['USA'], 'fullplot': '(T)ERROR is the first documentary to place filmmakers on the ground during an active FBI counterterrorism sting operation. Through the perspective of \"Shariff\", a 63-year-old Black revolutionary turned informant, viewers get an unfettered glimpse of the government\\'s counterterrorism tactics and the murky justifications behind them. Taut, stark and controversial, (T)ERROR illuminates the fragile relationships between individual and surveillance state in modern America, and asks who is watching the watchers.', 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2015, 1, 24, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Lyric R. Cabral', 'David Felix Sutcliffe'], 'awards': {'wins': 2, 'nominations': 3, 'text': '2 wins & 3 nominations.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-30 00:00:11.400000000', 'year': 2015, 'imdb': {'rating': 7.6, 'votes': 58, 'id': 4370922}, 'type': 'movie'}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13f7f29313caabde68f4'), 'plot': \"Set in early 19th century Wallachia, when a local policeman, Costandin, is hired by Iordache, a boyar (local noble), to find Garfin, a Gypsy slave who had run away from the boyar's estate ...\", 'genres': ['Adventure', 'Comedy', 'Drama'], 'runtime': 108, 'metacritic': 90, 'cast': ['Teodor Corban', 'Mihai Comanoiu', 'Toma Cuzin', 'Alexandru Dabija'], 'num_mflix_comments': 1, 'poster': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BNTgxNjA5MDkzNF5BMl5BanBnXkFtZTgwMTUyNzA5NDE@._V1_SY1000_SX677_AL_.jpg', 'title': 'Aferim!', 'fullplot': \"Set in early 19th century Wallachia, when a local policeman, Costandin, is hired by Iordache, a boyar (local noble), to find Garfin, a Gypsy slave who had run away from the boyar's estate after having an affair with his wife, Sultana. Costandin sets out to find the fugitive, beginning a journey full of adventures. Gypsy slavery lasted from the 14th century up until the middle of the 19th century, a situation which is very little known and almost nonexistent in the public debate today, although its impact continues to influence Romania's social life.\", 'languages': ['Romanian', 'Turkish', 'Romany'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2015, 3, 6, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Radu Jude'], 'writers': ['Radu Jude (screenplay)', 'Florin Lazarescu'], 'awards': {'wins': 4, 'nominations': 1, 'text': '4 wins & 1 nomination.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-08-19 00:44:09.953000000', 'year': 2015, 'imdb': {'rating': 8.3, 'votes': 1125, 'id': 4374460}, 'countries': ['Romania', 'Bulgaria', 'Czech Republic', 'France'], 'type': 'movie'}\n",
            "{'_id': ObjectId('573a13f7f29313caabde6d4d'), 'plot': \"An experimental documentary that explores Saudi Arabia's relationship with the U.S. and the role this has played in the war in Afghanistan.\", 'genres': ['Documentary'], 'runtime': 136, 'cast': ['Joanne Herring', 'Hamid Karzai', 'Mike Martin'], 'num_mflix_comments': 1, 'title': 'Adam Curtis: Bitter Lake', 'fullplot': \"Politicians used to have the confidence to tell us stories that made sense of the chaos of world events. But now there are no big stories and politicians react randomly to every new crisis - leaving us bewildered and disorientated. Bitter Lake is a new, adventurous and epic film by Adam Curtis that explains why the big stories that politicians tell us have become so simplified that we can't really see the world any longer. The narrative goes all over the world, America, Britain, Russia and Saudi Arabia - but the country at the heart of it is Afghanistan. Because Afghanistan is the place that has confronted our politicians with the terrible truth - that they cannot understand what is going on any longer. The film reveals the forces that over the past thirty years rose up and undermined the confidence of politics to understand the world. And it shows the strange, dark role that Saudi Arabia has played in this. But Bitter Lake is also experimental. Curtis has taken the unedited rushes of everything that the BBC has ever shot in Afghanistan - and used them in new and radical ways. He has tried to build a different and more emotional way of depicting what really happened in Afghanistan. A counterpoint to the thin, narrow and increasingly destructive stories told by those in power today.\", 'languages': ['English'], 'released': datetime.datetime(2015, 1, 25, 0, 0), 'directors': ['Adam Curtis'], 'writers': ['Adam Curtis'], 'awards': {'wins': 1, 'nominations': 0, 'text': '1 win.'}, 'lastupdated': '2015-09-14 23:36:33.993000000', 'year': 2015, 'imdb': {'rating': 8.1, 'votes': 802, 'id': 4393514}, 'countries': ['UK'], 'type': 'movie'}\n",
